WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:18.017 --> 00:19.853
EPISODE 11

00:22.897 --> 00:25.025
Damn, why is it taking so long?

00:27.110 --> 00:29.529
Our reservation's at 5:00 p.m.
We still have an hour.

00:30.321 --> 00:32.490
Why do you suddenly have to
look at houses now?

00:32.574 --> 00:35.744
I was planning to move near the hospital
before starting my fellowship.

00:35.827 --> 00:36.995
I mean,

00:37.579 --> 00:39.706
we're so busy
we barely see each other at home.

00:39.789 --> 00:41.124
We always see each other at work.

00:46.713 --> 00:48.298
Do you like me that much?

00:50.592 --> 00:52.218
Yes. So what?

00:54.888 --> 00:55.972
I like you a lot too.

00:59.309 --> 01:00.935
Did you just say that?

01:02.479 --> 01:03.938
Ever since we started dating,

01:04.022 --> 01:07.400
did you know we've been
really awkward and uncomfortable at home?

01:07.484 --> 01:10.403
That's not true.
It's been really comfortable and nice.

01:11.696 --> 01:13.907
You don't wear
your old, worn-out shirt anymore,

01:13.990 --> 01:15.742
and you don't lie around on the sofa now.

01:16.326 --> 01:18.328
You come out and wash after I go to bed.

01:21.414 --> 01:24.125
Regardless of our siblings,
it's right that I move out.

01:26.878 --> 01:28.004
And if I find a house,

01:30.131 --> 01:31.758
we get a place to be alone together.

01:33.343 --> 01:34.427
Alone?

01:34.511 --> 01:35.595
Just the two of us?

01:37.347 --> 01:38.181
To do what?

01:42.060 --> 01:43.520
That's not what I meant.

01:43.603 --> 01:46.189
Let's sign the contract today
and move in next week.

01:47.065 --> 01:48.858
Geez, where is the real estate agent?

01:48.942 --> 01:51.402
We've been waiting for hours.

01:53.154 --> 01:54.489
I didn't mean to overhear.

01:55.990 --> 01:56.908
Hello.

01:56.991 --> 01:58.118
Hello.

01:58.743 --> 02:00.036
I'm also a client.

02:00.620 --> 02:02.288
He's out showing a house.

02:02.372 --> 02:03.248
He won't be long.

02:03.331 --> 02:05.333
I see. Thank you.

02:08.128 --> 02:09.295
What were you looking for?

02:11.381 --> 02:14.384
Well, a small apartment
on jeonse or wolse lease.

02:14.467 --> 02:17.053
Around 700 square feet or so?

02:17.137 --> 02:18.513
-Yes.
-I see.

02:22.058 --> 02:23.017
In which neighborhood?

02:27.147 --> 02:27.981
Pyeongbuk-dong…

02:28.064 --> 02:29.023
Pyeongbuk-dong?

02:29.607 --> 02:30.984
Where Jongno Yulje is?

02:31.067 --> 02:32.443
Yes.

02:34.612 --> 02:36.239
That neighborhood's really nice.

02:37.282 --> 02:39.284
It has a lot of places
to visit nearby too,

02:39.367 --> 02:41.202
so there's no better place for newlyweds.

02:41.870 --> 02:43.580
We're not newlyweds.

02:43.663 --> 02:45.123
I'm sorry.

02:45.790 --> 02:48.835
You two just look so good together,

02:48.918 --> 02:49.794
so I just assumed.

02:51.963 --> 02:54.090
I know that neighborhood well.

02:54.173 --> 02:56.968
There's a place called
the Melodium Apartments there.

02:57.051 --> 02:59.554
It's a good location,
and the landscaping's well done too.

02:59.637 --> 03:01.347
Also, it's an "AWE."

03:01.431 --> 03:02.724
An AWE?

03:02.807 --> 03:04.684
"Apartment with an elementary school."

03:04.767 --> 03:06.477
It's a great place for raising children.

03:07.061 --> 03:08.021
Children?

03:09.522 --> 03:10.982
Never mind the AWE.

03:12.025 --> 03:13.693
And the land must have good energy too.

03:13.776 --> 03:15.570
Everyone ends up better off
after moving in.

03:15.653 --> 03:18.114
Especially, Building 215.

03:18.197 --> 03:20.116
The units face south,
so they get a lot of sun.

03:20.199 --> 03:22.118
And their structure
makes them well-ventilated.

03:24.412 --> 03:25.955
And it's on a great floor.

03:26.497 --> 03:29.167
The 12th floor is in the middle.
There's no noise between floors.

03:29.250 --> 03:31.419
And the neighbors are so nice.

03:31.502 --> 03:32.462
Plus,

03:33.546 --> 03:34.881
it's cheaper than what's nearby.

03:42.347 --> 03:43.181
About this much.

03:45.808 --> 03:48.561
But if it's that good, why is it cheap?

03:48.645 --> 03:51.522
The owner of the unit is nice, and…

03:52.148 --> 03:53.066
They're in a hurry.

03:53.900 --> 03:56.402
How about it? Want to go now?
You can see it right away.

03:57.612 --> 03:58.446
Are you?

03:58.529 --> 04:00.949
Yes, I'm the owner. It's my house.

04:01.866 --> 04:02.825
I knew it.

04:03.618 --> 04:05.578
I watch the news too, okay?

04:08.122 --> 04:09.540
I'm not that kind of person!

04:10.333 --> 04:12.710
I know we just met,
so I'm sorry to say this,

04:12.794 --> 04:14.587
but I was a victim.

04:15.213 --> 04:17.590
Yes, a victim of jeonse fraud.

04:17.674 --> 04:19.842
I suffered so much
because of that back then.

04:20.551 --> 04:22.220
Seriously, my wife was so--

04:22.303 --> 04:23.346
I assume she was very ill.

04:23.429 --> 04:25.598
So, she had to go to the hospital
and have surgery.

04:26.474 --> 04:27.308
How did you know?

04:27.392 --> 04:29.852
It's the same story used
by the scammers I saw on the news.

04:33.481 --> 04:34.857
After I was scammed,

04:35.692 --> 04:37.318
I was so scared of jeonse leases

04:37.402 --> 04:39.195
I took out a loan
to pay for all of my house.

04:39.279 --> 04:41.197
I'll show you the title deed myself.

04:41.281 --> 04:43.116
I have no debts attached to it.

04:43.199 --> 04:44.492
I'll show you my ID,

04:44.575 --> 04:47.078
and I'm going to get
jeonse guarantee insurance.

04:47.161 --> 04:49.497
Wait a second. Wait!

04:49.580 --> 04:50.957
I'm really not a scammer.

04:51.040 --> 04:52.500
My home really is that nice, so--

04:52.583 --> 04:54.127
Please stop. Or I'll bite.

04:55.128 --> 04:55.962
No!

04:57.588 --> 04:58.423
She really will.

04:59.549 --> 05:00.550
We have things to do, so…

05:01.551 --> 05:03.428
Let's at least clear things up
before you go!

05:03.511 --> 05:04.345
Seriously?

05:04.887 --> 05:06.431
Calm down.

05:07.515 --> 05:08.349
All right.

05:12.312 --> 05:14.564
How in the world do I seem like a scammer?

05:14.647 --> 05:16.107
I look like a saint.

05:19.319 --> 05:20.194
Sir.

05:20.278 --> 05:22.780
Hey. It was a long wait, wasn't it?
I'm sorry.

05:23.573 --> 05:25.491
No one's coming to see my house.

05:25.575 --> 05:27.285
I really have to move.

05:27.368 --> 05:29.203
Gosh, it's not something I can control.

05:29.287 --> 05:32.415
It's already been three months
since I put it on the market.

05:32.498 --> 05:35.418
We have to move
before my second child is born.

05:35.501 --> 05:37.045
All right. Just wait.

05:37.879 --> 05:40.631
Come on. Please, sir.

05:40.715 --> 05:42.175
What's wrong with you?

05:57.231 --> 05:58.858
We almost got scammed earlier.

06:00.234 --> 06:01.986
I'm eating out of shock.

06:02.070 --> 06:05.239
Right. You have to eat a lot
after being shocked.

06:05.323 --> 06:06.574
You have to calm yourself down.

06:08.409 --> 06:09.243
Eat up.

06:10.453 --> 06:11.287
Okay.

06:17.168 --> 06:18.044
What's this?

06:19.045 --> 06:20.421
What did you get on your hand?

06:21.172 --> 06:25.134
Gosh, your hands are so messy. Geez.

06:25.843 --> 06:26.761
There. It's all clean.

06:35.895 --> 06:37.313
My ring finger's a size ten.

06:38.272 --> 06:39.857
My fingers are thinner than you think.

06:39.941 --> 06:43.111
So stop that and just eat. Now.

06:44.612 --> 06:47.907
I have no idea what you're talking about.

06:47.990 --> 06:50.660
You had something on your finger,
so I really wiped it for you.

06:50.743 --> 06:52.120
Was that for buying couple rings?

06:52.203 --> 06:53.037
As a surprise?

06:53.788 --> 06:55.331
What? No!

06:55.414 --> 06:56.874
Why measure my finger suddenly then?

06:56.958 --> 06:57.792
And why secretly?

06:58.334 --> 07:00.086
Can't you just pretend not to know?

07:04.423 --> 07:05.716
I have something for you.

07:09.929 --> 07:10.763
Ta-da.

07:10.847 --> 07:11.681
What is this?

07:16.686 --> 07:17.728
These are nice!

07:18.521 --> 07:19.772
How did you know my size?

07:20.398 --> 07:22.066
I just knew without having to measure.

07:22.150 --> 07:22.984
But how?

07:24.360 --> 07:25.736
We use the same shoe cabinet.

07:26.988 --> 07:27.822
Right.

07:28.781 --> 07:29.615
Try them on.

07:43.754 --> 07:44.797
What's this?

07:46.716 --> 07:48.342
-Dad!
-Honey!

07:49.886 --> 07:51.387
-What's wrong?
-Dad!

07:52.013 --> 07:53.431
Someone help!

07:54.640 --> 07:55.641
Honey!

07:56.267 --> 07:58.394
What's wrong?
Is something caught in your throat?

07:58.478 --> 07:59.312
-The meat.
-Meat.

07:59.395 --> 08:01.022
He was eating meat and suddenly…

08:04.192 --> 08:05.902
-Dad!
-Call an ambulance! Hurry!

08:05.985 --> 08:07.069
Grab onto him.

08:09.530 --> 08:11.407
Sir, can you hear me?

08:11.491 --> 08:12.325
Sir!

08:15.995 --> 08:17.747
-Maintain his airway.
-Okay.

08:25.213 --> 08:26.589
An ambulance is on the way.

08:30.259 --> 08:31.761
-A spoon, please.
-Spoon…

08:44.690 --> 08:45.525
Wait.

08:49.320 --> 08:50.863
We have ROSC.

08:52.657 --> 08:54.867
Sir, can you hear me?

09:01.040 --> 09:03.834
The ambulance will arrive soon
to take you to the hospital.

09:04.377 --> 09:06.462
You'll be all right. Don't worry.

09:06.546 --> 09:07.713
It's here!

09:08.422 --> 09:09.590
Over here!

09:10.216 --> 09:11.342
Honey. Are you okay?

09:13.302 --> 09:14.303
Thank you.

09:14.387 --> 09:15.429
This way! Here!

09:18.307 --> 09:19.433
Thank goodness.

09:19.976 --> 09:21.727
He's okay! What a relief!

09:22.353 --> 09:23.854
Thank goodness it came quickly.

09:31.195 --> 09:34.407
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

09:34.490 --> 09:36.284
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

09:40.955 --> 09:42.707
I told you to get another hour of sleep.

09:42.790 --> 09:45.042
We have no time to meet this week.

09:45.126 --> 09:46.669
So we have to go to work together.

09:48.296 --> 09:50.172
Do you have time for coffee?

09:51.340 --> 09:53.426
At around 6:15 a.m.

09:58.806 --> 10:00.266
You washed your face, right?

10:00.349 --> 10:02.810
I couldn't. I can do it here.

10:07.189 --> 10:08.024
You're so cute.

10:09.692 --> 10:10.860
Excuse me.

10:15.615 --> 10:16.449
Yes?

10:17.199 --> 10:19.994
May I ask which floor
outpatient care is on?

10:20.077 --> 10:21.412
Oh, it's…

10:23.956 --> 10:25.249
It's on the second floor.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.251
You can take the elevator there.

10:28.085 --> 10:29.462
Okay, thank you.

10:48.481 --> 10:52.360
I'm Lee Chae-ryeong. I'm the new nurse
assigned to the delivery room.

10:52.443 --> 10:53.569
It's nice to meet you.

10:55.404 --> 10:56.697
It's nice to meet you too.

10:56.781 --> 11:00.493
If you have any questions,
you can ask our first-year residents.

11:00.576 --> 11:02.119
Yes, you can ask us anything.

11:02.203 --> 11:04.914
Like the hospital layout
or people's names,

11:04.997 --> 11:06.290
I'll tell you all I know.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.249
Thank you.

11:07.333 --> 11:10.169
I did come early to have a look around,

11:10.252 --> 11:11.545
but I think I'll get lost a lot.

11:11.629 --> 11:13.673
How early did you come in for work?

11:14.340 --> 11:15.883
Gosh, you're so diligent.

11:16.467 --> 11:18.677
I'll be even more diligent and work hard.

11:18.761 --> 11:19.929
Thank you for welcoming me.

11:20.012 --> 11:22.390
Let's grab a bite soon.

11:22.473 --> 11:23.891
-Sure.
-See you later.

11:24.892 --> 11:26.811
-It's nice to meet you.
-Let's get lunch later.

11:45.079 --> 11:46.956
It's nice to see you again, Doctor.

11:48.124 --> 11:49.625
Yes, me too.

11:51.043 --> 11:52.378
Don't worry about earlier.

11:52.962 --> 11:53.838
It's a secret, right?

11:53.921 --> 11:56.132
Yes, for now.

11:57.258 --> 11:58.092
Right.

12:01.220 --> 12:04.473
I was so shocked earlier
and couldn't tell you, but--

12:04.557 --> 12:05.891
I heard the new nurse is here?

12:12.523 --> 12:14.442
Hello, I'm Lee Chae-ryeong.

12:14.525 --> 12:15.568
It's nice to meet you.

12:17.570 --> 12:18.404
Hello.

12:19.613 --> 12:20.739
It's nice to meet you.

12:24.702 --> 12:26.120
I got some coffee.

12:26.203 --> 12:27.413
Thank you.

12:32.668 --> 12:34.336
I should…

12:35.212 --> 12:36.213
Have a nice day.

12:43.345 --> 12:44.388
Hello, Doctor.

12:47.808 --> 12:49.268
What is it? Where are you going?

12:49.351 --> 12:50.895
I heard the new nurse was here.

12:51.479 --> 12:52.855
She's at the station. Go say hi.

12:52.938 --> 12:55.065
Okay. But where are you going?

12:55.149 --> 12:55.983
Outpatient care.

12:58.819 --> 12:59.820
Outpatient care?

13:00.863 --> 13:01.697
Alone?

13:02.865 --> 13:03.949
Yeah. Who would I go with?

13:04.033 --> 13:05.075
I know, right?

13:06.243 --> 13:08.078
I mean, it just seems like

13:08.704 --> 13:10.706
you've been going there
day and night these days.

13:10.789 --> 13:13.125
I was wondering
if something nice was going on there.

13:13.209 --> 13:14.376
What are you talking about?

13:15.753 --> 13:18.255
Doctor, don't worry.

13:18.339 --> 13:19.548
I may not seem like it,

13:19.632 --> 13:21.759
but I'm very loyal.

13:29.141 --> 13:30.184
What's with him?

13:37.983 --> 13:38.984
Does he…

13:40.694 --> 13:42.238
Did you hear about Prof. Seo?

13:42.905 --> 13:45.449
The intern she put her time into
refused to shake her hand.

13:45.533 --> 13:47.117
She must've been rejected.

13:47.201 --> 13:48.410
Tak Gi-on?

13:48.494 --> 13:49.328
Yeah.

13:49.870 --> 13:52.540
The okay ones seem to have
already chosen their departments.

13:52.623 --> 13:54.333
Dong-eun's long gone too.

13:55.167 --> 13:57.503
So Gi-on's the only one we can hope for.

13:57.586 --> 14:00.422
I don't think he's interested in OB-GYN.

14:00.506 --> 14:03.759
And I'm not sure
if he's even that good at the job.

14:03.842 --> 14:07.012
But he is.
Prof. Geum told us at the team dinner.

14:07.096 --> 14:10.099
The intern on rotation for two months
was better than the first-years…

14:13.686 --> 14:15.938
is something that can't be true.

14:16.814 --> 14:17.648
But…

14:19.066 --> 14:21.443
Maybe she said it was nice?

14:21.527 --> 14:22.653
What did she say?

14:24.697 --> 14:25.573
Right.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.492
But, Doctor,

14:29.326 --> 14:31.829
what if no one joins OB-GYN next year?

14:32.538 --> 14:33.622
What do you think?

14:34.206 --> 14:35.082
We'll be screwed.

14:35.791 --> 14:36.792
Remember Pediatrics?

14:36.876 --> 14:38.335
That could be us.

14:39.211 --> 14:40.546
Our workload would double,

14:40.629 --> 14:42.756
and our days without sleep
would quadruple.

14:43.424 --> 14:46.218
Basically, your second year
would be doomed.

14:46.302 --> 14:47.970
Wait, do you mean

14:48.053 --> 14:50.514
if we have no first-years,
we'd have to do all the work?

14:50.598 --> 14:51.557
That's right.

14:51.640 --> 14:54.143
That's ridiculous. That's not fair.

14:54.852 --> 14:56.604
So, I wanted to tell you

14:56.687 --> 14:59.565
we should bring Tak Gi-on to our team.

14:59.648 --> 15:01.358
Let's try to persuade him, okay?

15:06.071 --> 15:07.239
INTERN TAK GI-ON

15:09.158 --> 15:09.992
Okay.

15:10.993 --> 15:12.244
I'll try to persuade him.

15:16.373 --> 15:18.792
Hello? Hi, Dr. Tak.

15:19.418 --> 15:21.253
-How does it feel here?
-It's okay.

15:22.838 --> 15:23.923
-And here?
-That's a bit--

15:24.006 --> 15:25.299
Excuse me.

15:27.259 --> 15:28.969
Is the patient with menstrual cramps here?

15:29.053 --> 15:29.887
Yes.

15:30.387 --> 15:31.305
Hello.

15:32.014 --> 15:33.641
Are you in a lot of pain, ma'am?

15:33.724 --> 15:34.642
Yes.

15:35.267 --> 15:37.728
She's been on painkillers
since yesterday afternoon,

15:37.811 --> 15:39.229
but she says the pain has worsened.

15:40.856 --> 15:42.566
She's experiencing cramps,

15:42.650 --> 15:44.401
but it's not like the feeling of diarrhea.

15:44.485 --> 15:47.071
An unlike gastrospasms,
there's no pain in the upper abdomen.

15:48.197 --> 15:50.532
Also, it feels
as if her lower abdomen will give out,

15:50.616 --> 15:52.451
but she says it's not like a contusion.

15:52.534 --> 15:53.786
I see.

15:55.329 --> 15:58.666
Ma'am, is it an irritating ache
in the lower belly,

15:58.749 --> 16:01.418
like your organs
are being squeezed, right?

16:01.502 --> 16:02.962
Yes, that's right.

16:03.045 --> 16:05.547
A heavy, twisting pain in the lower belly

16:05.631 --> 16:08.300
that spreads out
making it hard to even sit?

16:08.384 --> 16:09.551
Yes.

16:09.635 --> 16:11.387
I'm in so much pain

16:11.470 --> 16:13.555
that I can't do anything right now.

16:13.639 --> 16:15.933
I have severe menstrual pain too,
so I know.

16:16.016 --> 16:18.727
Have you been bleeding more than usual?

16:20.646 --> 16:23.941
It was particularly heavy this time,
so it got on my clothes…

16:29.697 --> 16:32.032
I had to use
an overnight pad the first day.

16:34.535 --> 16:36.954
It could be due to endometriosis
or adenomyosis,

16:37.037 --> 16:38.998
so we'll do an ultrasound.

16:39.081 --> 16:39.957
Okay.

16:47.464 --> 16:49.925
They're just menstrual cramps,
so I prescribed painkillers.

16:50.634 --> 16:52.761
She can be discharged after resting a bit.

16:53.887 --> 16:55.305
Okay. Thank you.

16:56.348 --> 16:59.476
Even female doctors
who don't experience bad menstrual pain

16:59.560 --> 17:00.894
don't really get how it hurts.

17:01.520 --> 17:04.481
Some wonder why people
even come to the hospital,

17:04.565 --> 17:06.316
because theirs are never that bad.

17:07.693 --> 17:10.738
But some male doctors say you can tell
without having to experience it.

17:10.821 --> 17:14.283
They figure it must really hurt if people
come to the ER early in the morning.

17:14.867 --> 17:18.120
They say it must be so hard
to go through that every month.

17:21.248 --> 17:23.876
Sometimes, it seemed like
those who don't know

17:23.959 --> 17:27.796
could understand and empathize better.

17:31.050 --> 17:31.967
Maybe that's why

17:32.676 --> 17:35.179
the male doctors
in our department are much more liked.

17:35.262 --> 17:38.557
The mothers and patients
love Jae-il the most.

17:39.433 --> 17:41.935
And Prof. Ryu Jae-hui
is the superstar of our hospital.

17:44.563 --> 17:45.564
So what I mean is

17:46.523 --> 17:48.484
I hope you don't think
OB-GYN isn't for you

17:49.109 --> 17:51.570
just because you're a guy.

17:51.653 --> 17:52.488
Doctor?

17:52.571 --> 17:53.614
Yes?

17:54.239 --> 17:56.116
I'm not thinking about anything right now.

17:57.534 --> 17:58.660
I'm totally fine.

17:58.744 --> 18:00.454
It's not a subject I'm too interested in.

18:02.706 --> 18:03.791
Is that so?

18:04.416 --> 18:05.459
Thank you.

18:07.419 --> 18:08.295
Sure.

18:11.173 --> 18:13.342
Damn. I had a speech prepared.

18:19.598 --> 18:20.474
Gosh.

18:22.309 --> 18:24.436
Sorry, I'm still a first-year resident.

18:28.148 --> 18:29.900
The EBW's 3,200.

18:31.235 --> 18:32.986
Amniotic fluid levels are fine.

18:34.238 --> 18:36.615
The umbilical artery Doppler
looks good too.

18:36.698 --> 18:40.577
I'm also scheduled to have
a detailed brain ultrasound today.

18:50.796 --> 18:52.256
Gosh, it's taking too long.

18:54.258 --> 18:56.760
I don't have much experience
with the brain yet.

18:57.302 --> 18:59.388
I'll look at a bit more
and tell you. I'm sorry.

19:02.474 --> 19:03.308
That…

19:12.317 --> 19:14.153
That square thing is the CSP.

19:15.279 --> 19:18.073
You need to measure
from where the CSP is visible.

19:18.157 --> 19:20.993
Yes, I know that too, but…

19:24.371 --> 19:26.456
Where the atrium's at its largest

19:27.124 --> 19:28.876
and when the borders look clear,

19:28.959 --> 19:31.211
that's when you should measure.

19:33.672 --> 19:35.090
Keep it straight and try again.

19:35.674 --> 19:36.758
Yes, ma'am.

19:43.182 --> 19:44.057
Hey, Yi-young.

19:45.309 --> 19:48.687
You still take forever
to read an ultrasound.

19:48.770 --> 19:49.688
ULTRASOUND ROOM 5

19:49.771 --> 19:51.481
You struggled more than last week.

19:52.065 --> 19:53.233
I'm sorry, Professor.

19:53.317 --> 19:55.360
Like in my case… I mean,

19:56.236 --> 19:58.363
when they're almost due
like patient Geum Sae-byeok,

19:58.447 --> 20:00.574
even lying down
to get in position is tough.

20:00.657 --> 20:03.493
Precision and speed is crucial. Okay?

20:03.577 --> 20:04.995
Yes, Professor.

20:06.121 --> 20:07.039
Thank you, ma'am.

20:08.081 --> 20:10.751
But getting the right angle
is harder than you expect.

20:11.543 --> 20:14.796
You have to get the angle
as soon as the probe touches the abdomen.

20:14.880 --> 20:16.757
But that takes more
than practicing a few times.

20:17.299 --> 20:18.592
Let's try again tomorrow.

20:18.675 --> 20:20.844
Let's get it down
to three minutes tomorrow.

20:21.803 --> 20:22.638
Again? Tomorrow?

20:22.721 --> 20:24.473
What? You don't want to?

20:25.349 --> 20:27.935
I'm lending you my body to teach you,
but you don't want to?

20:28.018 --> 20:29.937
No, I do. It sounds good.

20:30.020 --> 20:30.896
Right?

20:30.979 --> 20:32.564
-See you tomorrow.
-Goodbye, ma'am.

20:40.614 --> 20:41.490
I'm coming now.

20:42.491 --> 20:44.451
Don't eat! Wait for me. I said I'm coming!

20:50.040 --> 20:52.167
You said you'd be quick.
What took you so long?

20:52.251 --> 20:54.336
I was about to keel over from hunger.

20:54.962 --> 20:56.463
Weren't ultrasounds done a while ago?

20:57.214 --> 20:58.924
They were, but then…

21:01.093 --> 21:03.095
Did you know Prof. Seo had a junior?

21:03.178 --> 21:06.556
Yeah. Her daughter's in middle school,
and I think her son's nine.

21:06.640 --> 21:07.933
No, not that kind of junior.

21:08.016 --> 21:09.810
You mean Prof. Geum, right?

21:09.893 --> 21:12.354
Yeah. She's due next week,
but she won't rest.

21:12.437 --> 21:13.313
She's worse than Seo.

21:13.397 --> 21:15.941
It's her first year as a professor.
She's full of passion.

21:16.024 --> 21:18.735
Whatever it may be,
overdoing anything's not good.

21:19.361 --> 21:20.696
People should know when to stop.

21:20.779 --> 21:23.615
I know. I don't want to learn,
but she insists on teaching me.

21:24.533 --> 21:25.951
You're so unlucky.

21:26.034 --> 21:27.619
How did you get an OB prof?

21:27.703 --> 21:29.955
She's a patient
but also your superior and professor.

21:31.623 --> 21:34.418
If you do her sutures wrong,
you'll hear about it for four years.

21:36.086 --> 21:37.337
Damn it.

21:37.421 --> 21:38.297
This is so annoying.

21:39.006 --> 21:40.590
Sounds like a headache, Yi-young.

21:42.050 --> 21:43.510
But this is really good.

21:44.261 --> 21:45.804
It tasted better last time.

21:45.887 --> 21:46.930
You've had this before?

21:47.014 --> 21:48.724
Yeah, with Jae-il last time.

21:48.807 --> 21:51.184
The two of you? Why?

21:51.268 --> 21:52.102
Where?

21:53.812 --> 21:55.022
Wait, does Jae-il like you?

21:55.105 --> 21:56.231
Are you two dating?

21:56.315 --> 21:57.274
This again?

21:57.357 --> 21:58.442
It's not like that.

21:58.525 --> 22:00.610
You two were fighting,
so he said to give you space,

22:00.694 --> 22:02.362
and we went to outpatient care to eat.

22:03.488 --> 22:04.740
Still, though.

22:04.823 --> 22:07.326
Why go there at night? You're not dating.

22:07.409 --> 22:09.077
There's no one there at night.

22:09.161 --> 22:12.331
No, there are people. Jae-il said he saw.

22:12.414 --> 22:13.248
He did?

22:13.874 --> 22:15.083
Who?

22:19.129 --> 22:20.005
I don't know.

22:21.006 --> 22:21.923
I didn't ask.

22:24.843 --> 22:25.927
Where's Jae-il?

22:26.011 --> 22:27.512
He's going to sleep after surgery.

22:27.596 --> 22:28.597
He hasn't slept in days.

22:40.942 --> 22:43.612
MEDICAL ATTIRE RECOMMENDATIONS
TO PREVENT INFECTIONS

23:11.515 --> 23:15.602
GUARDIAN WAITING ROOM

23:47.551 --> 23:48.635
Help!

23:48.718 --> 23:50.846
Someone help!

24:03.108 --> 24:04.192
Help.

24:10.740 --> 24:13.285
You know how sometimes
after laparoscopic surgery,

24:14.161 --> 24:16.663
patients say their legs feel numb
or even paralyzed?

24:16.746 --> 24:17.873
It's totally true.

24:17.956 --> 24:20.250
I still can't feel my leg.

24:21.626 --> 24:24.296
You had breakfast, coffee,
and went to the convenience store.

24:24.379 --> 24:26.173
Since we're done, I can go now, right?

24:27.048 --> 24:27.883
Wait.

24:31.511 --> 24:33.263
Could you give me my lab coat?

25:03.084 --> 25:03.919
Hey!

25:07.214 --> 25:08.381
I need those pens.

25:12.510 --> 25:14.346
That should do it, right? I'm going.

25:15.055 --> 25:17.432
Sa-bi, when will you be back?

25:17.515 --> 25:18.516
Around lunchtime?

25:19.100 --> 25:20.977
Or at 4:00 p.m. after surgery?

25:21.061 --> 25:22.062
I won't be back.

25:22.145 --> 25:23.313
Then what about lunch?

25:23.396 --> 25:24.564
You figure it out.

25:24.648 --> 25:26.024
I'm not eating today.

25:27.442 --> 25:29.861
I'm not good at using the wheelchair yet.

25:29.945 --> 25:31.321
I can't go to the cafeteria alone.

25:31.404 --> 25:33.531
All the patients manage fine on their own.

25:33.615 --> 25:34.532
Hey, come on.

25:38.161 --> 25:40.830
Fine! I'll call you after surgery.

25:40.914 --> 25:42.958
You have to come. I'll be waiting.

25:43.041 --> 25:44.000
I said fine!

25:45.627 --> 25:47.379
Jae-il, you're so annoying!

25:50.715 --> 25:51.549
Bye!

25:57.138 --> 25:57.973
You scared me!

26:03.311 --> 26:05.397
We need to check on Ms. Ku Yun-ja, right?

26:05.981 --> 26:06.815
Yes.

26:08.775 --> 26:12.070
There's nothing much
to be happy about today.

26:12.153 --> 26:13.488
But you're in a good mood.

26:13.571 --> 26:14.406
No, I'm not.

26:15.156 --> 26:19.411
I feel so much pain
and embarrassment right now,

26:20.287 --> 26:21.621
I can't even lift my face.

26:26.334 --> 26:27.168
Let's go.

26:32.257 --> 26:35.302
How did you get hurt at a hospital?

26:36.678 --> 26:39.222
Don't worry about me.
I'll bounce right back.

26:41.433 --> 26:43.393
After getting
anti-cancer treatment for a while,

26:43.476 --> 26:45.979
your hands and feet
might start to peel like this.

26:46.062 --> 26:47.981
I'll prescribe you some ointment.

26:48.565 --> 26:49.399
Okay.

26:51.234 --> 26:52.193
By the way,

26:52.277 --> 26:56.031
the others in my ward who I used to get
anti-cancer treatment with…

27:00.118 --> 27:03.330
Maybe their schedules
didn't work out this time?

27:04.956 --> 27:05.957
Starting from this round,

27:06.041 --> 27:07.959
maybe they're going
to a different hospital.

27:09.878 --> 27:11.421
You're a terrible liar.

27:12.922 --> 27:14.799
I heard they're all gone.

27:16.009 --> 27:16.843
Yes.

27:17.594 --> 27:18.511
So you've heard.

27:18.595 --> 27:22.015
Suk-ja sat over there,
and I heard she passed last month.

27:22.724 --> 27:24.642
And Geun-yeong from Namyangju

27:24.726 --> 27:26.895
passed after receiving
anti-cancer treatment.

27:28.104 --> 27:28.938
Yes.

27:29.647 --> 27:31.191
She developed acute sepsis.

27:32.609 --> 27:33.943
When I saw her last,

27:34.027 --> 27:37.238
she smiled brightly and waved at me.

27:37.322 --> 27:39.699
I knew her time was coming.

27:41.326 --> 27:44.621
But the size of your tumor
has gotten much smaller.

27:45.288 --> 27:46.623
This drug is working well.

27:47.791 --> 27:48.917
Really?

27:50.043 --> 27:52.587
You're not lying to me
just to make me feel better, right?

27:52.670 --> 27:54.214
Of course not.

27:54.297 --> 27:55.298
Why would I lie for no--

27:55.382 --> 27:57.342
You're weak because you haven't eaten!

27:57.967 --> 28:00.345
I'm going to rot away
when I'm dead anyway.

28:00.428 --> 28:03.431
Why do you keep telling me to eat?

28:05.266 --> 28:06.518
They're fighting again.

28:07.894 --> 28:09.020
You should go.

28:09.104 --> 28:11.231
Who else is going to stop them?

28:11.314 --> 28:12.190
All right.

28:12.273 --> 28:15.652
You have to eat to continue the treatment.

28:15.735 --> 28:17.487
It doesn't sit in my stomach well.

28:17.570 --> 28:19.781
I can't force it down
because you tell me to.

28:21.825 --> 28:23.076
My goodness.

28:23.159 --> 28:24.160
Hello.

28:24.953 --> 28:26.496
What's the issue today?

28:26.579 --> 28:29.624
You don't eat,
so that's why your illness came back.

28:30.458 --> 28:33.545
That's why I said to just leave me to die.

28:33.628 --> 28:35.088
I've had to hear that

28:35.797 --> 28:37.757
for over ten years!

28:38.550 --> 28:40.135
If you want to go that badly,

28:40.218 --> 28:42.971
don't make your own sister
suffer from taking care of you!

28:43.596 --> 28:46.099
Ma'am, are you having trouble eating?

28:46.182 --> 28:48.893
She's refused food since yesterday.

28:48.977 --> 28:51.020
They say she has to eat to be treated.

28:51.104 --> 28:53.106
But she won't listen to me.

28:54.232 --> 28:57.068
Ma'am, you have to eat well.

28:57.736 --> 29:00.613
We switched your meals to porridge
to make it easier to eat.

29:01.364 --> 29:03.199
You should eat well to start treatment

29:03.283 --> 29:05.034
so you can get well soon and go home.

29:05.910 --> 29:08.288
Yes, I have to go home.

29:08.997 --> 29:09.873
Seong-chan.

29:10.457 --> 29:12.542
Don't worry about me, son.

29:12.625 --> 29:16.713
You didn't have to bring
all these things here to the hospital.

29:16.796 --> 29:18.923
I'm sure you're busy with school as it is.

29:19.966 --> 29:22.177
There you go again.

29:22.260 --> 29:24.721
Yesterday, he was your dad and you wept.

29:24.804 --> 29:26.347
Today, he's your son?

29:27.474 --> 29:29.267
Your son Seong-chan

29:29.350 --> 29:32.937
was cared by his mother
for ten years before he passed.

29:33.605 --> 29:34.564
Did you forget?

29:36.816 --> 29:37.984
You awful brat.

29:38.735 --> 29:40.445
Don't say that in front of him.

29:41.404 --> 29:44.365
You're an adult in your fifties.
Don't say that to your nephew.

29:44.991 --> 29:45.950
Listen,

29:46.034 --> 29:49.454
I turned 70 a while ago. Okay?

29:49.537 --> 29:52.624
Geez, the old woman's
completely lost her mind.

29:55.210 --> 29:58.129
But you know why
your aunt's being like this, right?

29:58.713 --> 29:59.589
She's out of it.

30:00.757 --> 30:02.592
Yes, of course.

30:03.384 --> 30:05.136
Please eat your porridge today…

30:08.515 --> 30:09.474
Mother.

30:27.617 --> 30:30.662
Thank you for helping
with the surgery, Professor.

30:30.745 --> 30:33.414
Maybe I overdid it yesterday.
My stomach feels a bit tight.

30:34.123 --> 30:35.792
I only did the fundal.

30:36.501 --> 30:38.628
-But are you okay?
-Yes.

30:39.295 --> 30:40.421
I don't think so.

30:41.130 --> 30:42.966
She's had pain all morning,

30:43.049 --> 30:44.551
and she doesn't look so great.

30:46.010 --> 30:47.762
I think she's in labor for real,

30:47.846 --> 30:50.348
but she insists it's false labor
and keeps working.

30:51.474 --> 30:52.809
Wow, Yi-young,

30:52.892 --> 30:55.228
spoken like her attending doctor.

30:55.812 --> 30:58.731
Yes, but she won't listen to her doctor.

30:59.399 --> 31:01.192
All right, Dr. Oh.

31:01.276 --> 31:03.862
We did a study last time, right?

31:03.945 --> 31:07.532
False labor can sometimes
be as regular as true labor.

31:07.615 --> 31:09.909
But it's fading on its own right now.

31:10.535 --> 31:11.953
This is false labor.

31:14.789 --> 31:16.624
So you can still work a bit more?

31:16.708 --> 31:19.627
Yes, I have a pile of things
to get through right now.

31:19.711 --> 31:21.170
Next Wednesday is my due date,

31:21.254 --> 31:23.715
but I'm not sure if I can finish by then.

31:23.798 --> 31:25.967
Since you're always like this,

31:26.050 --> 31:27.594
this is why people keep asking

31:27.677 --> 31:29.554
if we're sisters.

31:29.637 --> 31:30.930
Really?

31:31.014 --> 31:33.141
That's a total compliment for me.

31:35.268 --> 31:37.395
You don't need to worry about me.

31:37.478 --> 31:40.148
I've handled so many deliveries
in my career.

31:40.231 --> 31:41.065
You know?

31:41.149 --> 31:43.276
"Oh, the cervix is about to open."

31:43.359 --> 31:46.195
"If I start pushing now,
the baby will be out in ten minutes."

31:46.279 --> 31:48.197
I know everything. Really.

31:48.281 --> 31:49.866
The VD simulation is over.

31:49.949 --> 31:53.244
You think delivering a patient's baby
is the same as having your own?

31:53.328 --> 31:55.747
I'm telling you.
Come see for yourself next week.

31:55.830 --> 31:57.832
You'll only have to cut the cord
when you arrive,

31:57.916 --> 31:59.918
because I'll have the baby
out and waiting.

32:00.001 --> 32:02.128
-Fine, so just get some rest now.
-Okay.

32:03.671 --> 32:05.965
You better not let
your water break in the OR

32:06.049 --> 32:07.800
and have to be dragged
to the delivery room.

32:07.884 --> 32:09.427
What kind of person would do that?

32:10.511 --> 32:13.097
What kind?
The kind who's been here this whole time.

32:14.515 --> 32:15.642
That's so cool.

32:16.351 --> 32:17.352
You're so cool!

32:17.936 --> 32:19.854
-Call me if you need help.
-I will.

32:19.938 --> 32:21.105
Nice work.

32:21.189 --> 32:22.023
Bye.

32:25.109 --> 32:26.194
Thank you, Professor.

32:32.784 --> 32:33.618
Are you okay?

32:34.243 --> 32:35.411
Should I call Prof. Seo back?

32:35.495 --> 32:36.329
No.

32:39.707 --> 32:40.583
At this rate,

32:41.626 --> 32:43.920
my due date might come earlier.

32:44.003 --> 32:45.380
By about a day at best.

32:46.589 --> 32:48.341
You know that?

32:48.424 --> 32:49.509
Of course.

32:49.592 --> 32:51.886
I've been doing this for years.
I just know.

32:53.638 --> 32:54.681
This is killing me.

32:56.432 --> 32:57.558
Yes, Professor?

32:58.893 --> 33:01.062
BP? All of a sudden? And the baby?

33:04.732 --> 33:05.775
There aren't any?

33:06.442 --> 33:07.735
Yes, I'll be right there.

33:10.571 --> 33:12.240
A surgery just came in.

33:12.323 --> 33:13.199
Again?

33:14.158 --> 33:15.827
You must be so tired.

33:15.910 --> 33:18.204
No, I'm just assisting. It's okay.

33:18.287 --> 33:19.706
I see. Assisting.

33:22.667 --> 33:23.835
Good luck then.

33:24.919 --> 33:25.920
Where are you going?

33:28.464 --> 33:29.882
I'm going to eat.

33:30.967 --> 33:34.303
They don't have a second assistant,
so I said you'd come too.

33:34.929 --> 33:35.805
Me?

33:36.931 --> 33:38.266
-Me too?
-Yeah.

33:38.349 --> 33:39.642
Shall we?

33:39.726 --> 33:40.560
It's urgent.

33:43.271 --> 33:44.272
Gosh, my back.

33:45.690 --> 33:46.691
It's fine.

33:48.026 --> 33:48.860
I'm fine.

33:49.819 --> 33:50.695
Thanks.

34:03.875 --> 34:05.460
You're writing a death certificate.

34:08.337 --> 34:09.172
Yes.

34:12.842 --> 34:15.762
Do you know why I chose OB-GYN?

34:17.513 --> 34:19.474
Instead of death certificates,

34:19.557 --> 34:21.392
I wanted to write birth certificates.

34:24.228 --> 34:27.148
And the only place in the hospital

34:27.231 --> 34:29.067
where people celebrate
and are happy about crying

34:29.609 --> 34:31.944
is OB-GYN.

34:33.362 --> 34:36.115
It's where a lot of great things happen.

34:36.199 --> 34:37.909
That's what I'm trying to say.

34:37.992 --> 34:38.868
Doctor.

34:38.951 --> 34:40.036
Yes?

34:41.037 --> 34:44.999
Up until today, I've written
only four death certificates.

34:47.627 --> 34:49.921
And two were from GYN.

34:51.964 --> 34:52.924
Is that so?

34:53.007 --> 34:54.801
One patient had late-stage cancer

34:54.884 --> 34:56.844
and passed
after just a few chemo sessions.

34:58.137 --> 35:00.848
The other was my age.
Her ovarian cancer recurred.

35:02.016 --> 35:03.017
When that happened,

35:05.436 --> 35:06.646
I really cried a lot.

35:09.857 --> 35:11.859
I see. That was GYN.

35:15.404 --> 35:16.697
I have to check on a patient.

35:17.740 --> 35:18.574
Have a nice day.

35:19.242 --> 35:20.201
All right.

35:20.993 --> 35:21.828
See you.

35:24.622 --> 35:26.207
He's smarter than I thought.

35:30.044 --> 35:32.380
Aren't sisters usually close though?

35:33.881 --> 35:34.757
I have a brother.

35:35.341 --> 35:36.843
Ask Yi-young about sisters.

35:36.926 --> 35:39.554
The patient in Room 1014 and her sister

35:39.637 --> 35:41.305
lived together their whole lives,

35:41.389 --> 35:43.224
but they fight so intensely,

35:43.307 --> 35:44.934
saying the other should die first.

35:45.017 --> 35:46.811
After taking care
of her sister for so long,

35:46.894 --> 35:48.354
the younger one seems exhausted.

35:48.437 --> 35:49.981
She's always very irritable.

35:51.232 --> 35:54.277
The saying, "Long-term illnesses
will wear anyone down," seems so sad.

35:58.322 --> 35:59.949
You can go by yourself from here, right?

36:00.032 --> 36:01.159
I'm leaving.

36:03.786 --> 36:05.288
Take me just up to the ward.

36:06.205 --> 36:08.583
My arms hurt so much
from pushing this thing.

36:15.506 --> 36:17.133
But I looked into it,

36:17.216 --> 36:19.802
and that kind of nerve compression
clears in two hours.

36:19.886 --> 36:21.470
That's a lie.

36:21.554 --> 36:22.471
I still can't move it.

36:23.347 --> 36:24.182
So I was thinking,

36:26.350 --> 36:27.476
can't we clock out together?

36:27.560 --> 36:29.520
-I'm going to read papers before I leave.
-Really?

36:29.604 --> 36:31.314
Really? I will too. Let's do it together.

36:33.941 --> 36:36.319
Actually, I'm going to review
surgery recordings instead.

36:36.986 --> 36:38.571
I was going to do that too.

36:38.654 --> 36:40.031
Want to watch together?

36:41.741 --> 36:43.534
Hey, do you…

36:45.119 --> 36:47.246
Ouch, that's hot!

36:53.002 --> 36:54.879
I can walk.

36:56.881 --> 36:59.050
Look. I wonder when it got better.

36:59.133 --> 37:00.009
This is amazing.

37:03.221 --> 37:04.597
I forgot I have to go to the ward.

37:04.680 --> 37:05.848
I'm late.

37:07.725 --> 37:09.435
Can you return that for me?

37:09.518 --> 37:10.394
Bye!

37:17.276 --> 37:19.695
Does he really like me?

37:20.613 --> 37:22.865
This isn't a bad thing.

37:22.949 --> 37:24.700
What's so good about that bed?

37:25.409 --> 37:27.411
Hello.

37:28.621 --> 37:29.830
Is something the matter?

37:29.914 --> 37:31.082
Doctor.

37:31.165 --> 37:33.167
Why does she have to move
next to the door?

37:34.001 --> 37:35.002
I already told her.

37:36.504 --> 37:38.005
Well,

37:38.089 --> 37:40.466
the bed remote and call bell are broken.

37:41.050 --> 37:43.386
So until we can get the bed fixed,

37:43.469 --> 37:45.638
the facilities team asked us to move.

37:45.721 --> 37:47.348
Can't she just use it?

37:49.850 --> 37:51.310
I don't want her to move.

37:51.394 --> 37:53.396
There might not be a window there,

37:53.479 --> 37:55.564
but we can come quicker to check her,

37:55.648 --> 37:57.942
it's closer to the bathroom,
and has many more benefits.

37:58.025 --> 38:01.070
My back's about to break
from taking care of her.

38:01.737 --> 38:04.782
I can't move this old woman on my own.

38:04.865 --> 38:07.201
I will help you with that.

38:07.285 --> 38:09.036
My leg's all better now too.

38:15.084 --> 38:17.586
I've been in hospitals for a long time,

38:17.670 --> 38:19.297
but this is a first.

38:20.089 --> 38:21.632
Can we just--

38:21.716 --> 38:24.510
Gosh, you talk too much, Mi-yeong.

38:24.593 --> 38:27.972
Just listen and do what he says, will you?

38:28.055 --> 38:31.392
Your brother-in-law's
always done the best for me.

38:31.475 --> 38:32.727
I've told you repeatedly

38:32.810 --> 38:35.146
he is the head of our household.

38:35.229 --> 38:36.522
He takes Father's place.

38:37.189 --> 38:40.609
A drunkard who led our family to ruin?
Head of the household, my foot.

38:41.277 --> 38:43.446
How can you still call him your husband?

38:43.529 --> 38:45.573
Gosh, I'm sorry.

38:46.198 --> 38:48.284
I should have married her off

38:48.367 --> 38:50.119
and sent her away.

38:51.037 --> 38:52.580
But what can I do?

38:52.663 --> 38:54.498
She's my only family.

38:56.042 --> 38:58.044
I hope you understand, dear.

38:58.127 --> 39:00.296
I'll talk to her.

39:02.089 --> 39:02.923
It's fine…

39:04.925 --> 39:07.928
My… dear.

39:09.013 --> 39:10.473
Thank you, dear.

39:24.111 --> 39:24.945
This.

39:25.654 --> 39:26.572
And this.

39:26.655 --> 39:28.366
-That's enough.
-And this.

39:30.117 --> 39:31.118
This.

39:31.202 --> 39:32.661
-Can you eat all of this?
-Go.

39:46.217 --> 39:47.218
What?

39:53.432 --> 39:55.476
But I'm not good at grilling.

39:55.559 --> 39:57.728
It's okay. It's impossible
to ruin the meat here.

40:01.565 --> 40:03.317
Do-won said he'd come,
but left me on read.

40:03.401 --> 40:04.902
He's in surgery.

40:05.694 --> 40:07.822
He's on call
and has a string of surgeries.

40:09.615 --> 40:11.742
Right, he didn't even have lunch.

40:11.826 --> 40:13.411
I bet he can't have dinner too.

40:17.164 --> 40:17.998
What?

40:18.624 --> 40:20.918
Since when did you
care so much about him eating?

40:21.836 --> 40:23.712
I know. And now that I think about it,

40:23.796 --> 40:28.551
last weekend, you insisted on bringing him
his socks and underwear yourself.

40:31.345 --> 40:32.596
By any chance…

40:38.769 --> 40:40.020
Did you borrow money from him?

40:41.272 --> 40:42.231
Are those new clothes?

40:45.443 --> 40:47.528
No. I've had this for a while.

40:47.611 --> 40:48.612
How much did you borrow?

40:49.405 --> 40:51.323
This isn't the first time, right?

40:51.407 --> 40:52.616
Are you serious?

40:52.700 --> 40:54.368
Here's your beer.

40:54.452 --> 40:55.494
Thank you.

40:57.288 --> 40:58.122
Answer me.

40:58.205 --> 40:59.373
I said I didn't.

40:59.457 --> 41:01.667
Instead of blaming the innocent,
just drink your beer.

41:01.750 --> 41:03.919
You're telling the truth, right?

41:04.003 --> 41:05.671
You better not ask him for money or else.

41:11.594 --> 41:13.846
Gosh, how long has it been
since you had beer?

41:15.723 --> 41:17.141
Six months.

41:17.975 --> 41:19.727
We're skipping the procedure this month,

41:20.311 --> 41:22.146
so I'm going to chug all the beer I want.

41:31.530 --> 41:32.531
That hits the spot.

41:34.492 --> 41:35.826
I'm so happy.

41:35.910 --> 41:37.995
How did you manage
without beer for six months?

41:38.078 --> 41:39.246
If only I could get pregnant,

41:39.330 --> 41:41.832
I'd quit drinking beer forever.

41:41.916 --> 41:44.335
But I'm not, so I have to keep drinking.

41:44.418 --> 41:46.003
I think one won't be enough.

41:47.087 --> 41:48.422
Excuse me! Could we have--

41:49.465 --> 41:51.592
-Are you okay? I'm sorry.
-Excuse me.

41:54.345 --> 41:55.304
Yi-young?

41:55.930 --> 41:56.972
What are you doing here?

41:57.640 --> 41:59.475
I'm eating out. You?

41:59.558 --> 42:01.018
Me? I'm…

42:03.270 --> 42:04.438
Hello.

42:05.022 --> 42:07.816
I'm Yi-young's friend, Pyo Nam-kyung.

42:08.526 --> 42:10.027
Oh, my. You're her friend?

42:11.320 --> 42:12.238
We're not friends.

42:12.863 --> 42:13.822
See you tomorrow.

42:18.661 --> 42:19.578
It's hot.

42:24.208 --> 42:26.293
Don't talk about Do-won.

42:38.180 --> 42:41.267
I hope I'm not cluelessly
imposing on a family dinner.

42:41.350 --> 42:42.268
You are.

42:43.060 --> 42:45.062
I was supposed to meet a friend here,

42:45.145 --> 42:47.314
but they suddenly said
they couldn't make it.

42:47.398 --> 42:49.316
I didn't want to eat here alone

42:49.400 --> 42:50.818
and was just about to leave.

42:51.402 --> 42:53.028
Thank you so much.

42:53.112 --> 42:54.863
We're the ones who are grateful.

42:54.947 --> 42:57.324
I've never had a meal
with a friend of Yi-young's before.

42:57.408 --> 42:58.367
It's so nice.

42:58.450 --> 42:59.577
I said we're not friends.

42:59.660 --> 43:02.413
Yi-young and I
went to the same high school.

43:02.496 --> 43:04.790
And we ended up at the same hospital.

43:04.873 --> 43:05.749
How cool is that?

43:05.833 --> 43:07.710
Wow, you two go way back!

43:08.502 --> 43:11.630
Please take good care of my sister-in-law.

43:13.215 --> 43:15.843
She's such a mess, so I worry about her.

43:16.552 --> 43:18.137
Is she doing okay?

43:20.180 --> 43:21.724
These days, Yi-young is…

43:21.807 --> 43:22.641
Don't.

43:24.268 --> 43:27.062
The professors praise her
for her accurate exams.

43:27.938 --> 43:29.106
And of all the first-years,

43:29.189 --> 43:30.858
she's the fastest ultrasound reader.

43:31.817 --> 43:32.651
Really?

43:33.319 --> 43:34.194
But the thing is

43:34.278 --> 43:36.363
she can never hold back
what she wants to say.

43:36.447 --> 43:38.532
And if you ask her
to do something she dislikes,

43:38.616 --> 43:40.075
her face turns so sour.

43:40.159 --> 43:42.244
So she's adjusted well to the work,

43:42.328 --> 43:44.663
but she's a bit lacking in social skills.

43:46.832 --> 43:50.377
Still, I thought she'd be bad at both.
So it's such a relief.

43:50.919 --> 43:52.588
Great job, Yi-young.

43:52.671 --> 43:54.590
That's more than what we expected.

43:56.842 --> 43:58.761
Please look out for her.

43:58.844 --> 44:01.430
If she gets fired again,
she has nowhere to go.

44:02.222 --> 44:04.016
Yes, I'll take good care of her.

44:04.099 --> 44:06.101
Don't worry, Joo-young.

44:07.561 --> 44:10.147
Since when were you two
such close friends? Geez.

44:10.230 --> 44:11.982
Yeah, eat up.

44:13.025 --> 44:15.319
-Thank you.
-She said "Joo-young."

44:16.654 --> 44:17.738
She's a good eater.

44:18.447 --> 44:19.865
That's so nice to see.

44:22.618 --> 44:23.619
Wait.

44:24.912 --> 44:27.247
You look a lot like someone I know.

44:28.874 --> 44:30.125
Doesn't he look so similar?

44:31.502 --> 44:32.753
What? I don't know.

44:32.836 --> 44:34.338
I mean, his…

44:35.589 --> 44:37.299
He has the same eyes and mouth!

44:38.133 --> 44:39.843
Oh, my! Who was it?

44:39.927 --> 44:41.053
He's…

44:44.515 --> 44:45.683
Professor Jo Joon-mo!

44:47.768 --> 44:50.229
If I didn't know,
I'd totally think they were brothers.

44:51.021 --> 44:52.272
You look so much like him.

44:53.524 --> 44:55.067
He must be really handsome then.

44:57.611 --> 44:58.695
They're not similar at all.

44:59.279 --> 45:00.322
We're all done, so get up.

45:00.406 --> 45:02.449
Really? Let me get some more of this.

45:02.533 --> 45:03.659
No, let's go home.

45:03.742 --> 45:05.577
Can I just have one more plate?

45:05.661 --> 45:07.621
You ate everything! Don't you have work?

45:07.704 --> 45:09.498
-What's with you?
-I'll only be ten minutes.

45:09.581 --> 45:10.958
Ten minutes, my foot. Put it down.

45:13.710 --> 45:15.045
-Fine, eat.
-Yes.

45:20.676 --> 45:21.510
Hey, Jae-il.

45:25.013 --> 45:25.848
Hi.

45:25.931 --> 45:26.974
Aren't you buying coffee?

45:27.057 --> 45:28.392
No, I was just passing by.

45:28.475 --> 45:29.768
I see. Wait.

45:29.852 --> 45:31.061
I have something to tell you.

45:32.980 --> 45:33.814
Well--

45:33.897 --> 45:35.983
Dr. Kim's sending
thank you gifts for the wedding.

45:36.733 --> 45:38.819
It's food,
so they'll be sent to our homes.

45:38.902 --> 45:40.654
Can you collect the professors' addresses?

45:40.737 --> 45:42.698
I'll do from the fellows
to the first-years.

45:44.116 --> 45:44.950
Okay.

45:45.033 --> 45:45.868
And…

45:47.911 --> 45:48.745
What now?

45:49.997 --> 45:51.165
I looked into it,

45:51.999 --> 45:54.168
and sudden leg paralysis
has no aftereffects.

45:55.878 --> 45:58.755
I did feel some pain yesterday.

46:01.049 --> 46:02.384
But it feels totally fine today.

46:02.468 --> 46:03.635
It looked fine yesterday too.

46:04.219 --> 46:05.971
You said it was numb and weak,

46:06.054 --> 46:07.598
but you sprang up and ran.

46:07.681 --> 46:10.184
-When did I ever run?
-You did.

46:10.267 --> 46:11.643
I walked slowly.

46:11.727 --> 46:15.063
No, I tried to follow with the wheelchair,
but you were so fast I couldn't.

46:15.147 --> 46:17.274
Gosh, you and your blasted memory.

46:18.775 --> 46:20.611
I don't know why I did that either, okay?

46:22.362 --> 46:24.239
Can you just forget it and let it go?

46:24.781 --> 46:26.617
You're making me awkward
by poking and prying.

46:27.367 --> 46:30.078
I was just worried you might be in pain.

46:32.539 --> 46:33.457
Worried?

46:33.540 --> 46:34.374
Yeah.

46:35.083 --> 46:35.918
But you still fuss.

46:37.961 --> 46:38.962
Were you really worried?

46:40.380 --> 46:41.298
You kept worrying?

46:43.258 --> 46:44.092
Doctor.

46:45.427 --> 46:46.595
Prof. Geum's baby…

46:52.935 --> 46:53.852
Hey.

46:53.936 --> 46:54.853
Hello.

46:57.648 --> 46:58.524
Professor.

46:59.566 --> 47:01.735
Why didn't you call me?
I can do that for you.

47:01.818 --> 47:03.028
I needed to use the bathroom.

47:03.862 --> 47:05.280
I can put on NST monitors.

47:05.364 --> 47:06.949
I can do it in my sleep.

47:10.911 --> 47:12.371
I flashed on the monitor, didn't I?

47:13.038 --> 47:13.914
I'm sorry.

47:13.997 --> 47:15.666
It's okay as long as you're fine.

47:20.212 --> 47:21.755
How's the pain?

47:21.838 --> 47:23.215
The same as when I was admitted.

47:23.298 --> 47:26.051
Contractions are regular
at five to seven-minute intervals.

47:33.100 --> 47:34.977
Are you in pain? Where?

47:37.229 --> 47:38.438
Do you want the epidural now?

47:38.522 --> 47:39.773
No.

47:42.276 --> 47:44.194
Let's do another exam and then decide.

47:44.278 --> 47:45.404
Okay.

47:56.957 --> 47:58.041
I'm sorry.

48:00.460 --> 48:01.628
I'm still at 2.0, right?

48:01.712 --> 48:03.380
Yes, your pelvic exam shows a 2.0,

48:03.463 --> 48:04.548
and station is high.

48:06.174 --> 48:07.509
I was admitted two hours ago,

48:08.260 --> 48:11.138
but there's no change
in contractions or the cervix.

48:11.221 --> 48:13.223
So let's wait a bit longer
for the epidural.

48:13.890 --> 48:16.310
But if it hurts a lot,
do you want some painkillers?

48:17.019 --> 48:18.478
I have to bear it for it to open.

48:19.354 --> 48:22.691
In three hours, we can check again,

48:22.774 --> 48:25.986
and decide on the oxytocin then.

48:26.570 --> 48:27.404
Okay.

48:28.822 --> 48:30.657
If the pain's too much, please call me.

48:30.741 --> 48:31.742
I'm fine.

48:32.367 --> 48:34.328
Use your time to check
on other patients instead.

48:36.413 --> 48:38.248
You know Ms. Joo Ha-na on POD 2?

48:38.332 --> 48:41.043
Her CBC results are out,
so can you check and tell me?

48:41.126 --> 48:43.712
I couldn't check
because I was suddenly admitted.

48:43.795 --> 48:46.048
You can't check patients in this state.

48:46.131 --> 48:47.049
So you don't want to?

48:48.050 --> 48:49.009
It's not that…

48:49.092 --> 48:51.053
I guess I should go check it myself then.

48:51.136 --> 48:53.680
-Can you undo this?
-No!

48:53.764 --> 48:54.640
No.

48:55.307 --> 48:56.850
I'll check and update you.

48:56.933 --> 48:57.976
-Yeah?
-Yes.

48:58.060 --> 49:00.312
Okay. Thank you, Dr. Oh.

49:00.395 --> 49:01.480
Go and check.

49:03.273 --> 49:04.107
Go on.

49:11.239 --> 49:13.408
Stop eating!

49:13.492 --> 49:16.578
Why are you eating so much
all of a sudden?

49:19.373 --> 49:22.167
You complained like hell
about not eating before.

49:22.250 --> 49:24.586
Now, you're complaining like hell
about eating too much?

49:24.670 --> 49:28.090
I'm worried you might get
indigestion again!

49:28.173 --> 49:30.092
They have medication for that.

49:30.676 --> 49:33.387
After I eat,
I'm taking a lap around the ward.

49:34.429 --> 49:37.057
You're going to walk?
You have the strength to do so?

49:37.140 --> 49:38.058
Of course.

49:38.809 --> 49:39.685
Hello.

49:41.770 --> 49:43.063
The doctor's here.

49:43.897 --> 49:45.482
I'm here to receive your consent.

49:46.191 --> 49:47.651
You finished all your food today.

49:47.734 --> 49:49.736
You look nice today, Doctor.

49:50.320 --> 49:51.905
Did something good happen?

49:53.615 --> 49:55.867
Am I the handsome Jae-il today, ma'am?

49:56.493 --> 49:58.829
Hold on. What's suddenly gotten into her?

49:59.579 --> 50:02.416
She's eating well, and she's lucid.

50:02.499 --> 50:04.626
I don't know where she got the strength.

50:04.710 --> 50:05.961
She wants to go exercise.

50:06.044 --> 50:08.505
It's because she received
an albumin injection,

50:08.588 --> 50:10.549
and her condition's much better now.

50:10.632 --> 50:11.758
Her numbers look good too.

50:11.842 --> 50:13.760
Just yesterday, she said she was dying.

50:13.844 --> 50:16.471
Why is she suddenly so energetic today?

50:16.555 --> 50:18.056
What good would that do?

50:18.140 --> 50:18.974
But

50:19.766 --> 50:20.767
that's good news.

50:21.435 --> 50:23.603
Why are you upset, ma'am?

50:23.687 --> 50:25.313
No, it's not that…

50:28.191 --> 50:29.192
It's nothing.

50:29.735 --> 50:32.487
If she's more energetic,
she'll do better when receiving treatment

50:32.571 --> 50:33.822
and recover faster.

50:35.490 --> 50:36.742
But what brings you here?

50:36.825 --> 50:39.411
We'll administer
an anti-cancer drug later,

50:39.494 --> 50:42.205
but as I explained before,
we changed it to a new drug.

50:42.289 --> 50:43.874
So you need to sign a new consent form.

50:43.957 --> 50:45.000
Should I explain it again?

50:45.083 --> 50:46.752
Gosh, I know everything.

50:48.128 --> 50:48.962
Here you go.

50:51.339 --> 50:54.092
I'm sick of hearing that explanation.

50:56.303 --> 50:57.262
Thank you.

51:06.813 --> 51:08.607
She was sent to the ER just now.

51:08.690 --> 51:09.983
She's not our patient,

51:10.066 --> 51:12.486
she has ROM with labor, but it's mild.

51:12.569 --> 51:14.654
-So it's not a super emergency.
-No.

51:14.738 --> 51:16.656
-Tak Gi-on's there, right?
-Yes.

51:16.740 --> 51:18.909
Let's be calm and steady with him. Okay?

51:18.992 --> 51:20.285
Like it's no big deal.

51:20.368 --> 51:22.954
-So we seem free and graceful.
-Right.

51:23.038 --> 51:25.123
Don't forget. Gi-on is watching.

51:25.207 --> 51:26.500
Okay, I won't.

51:26.583 --> 51:27.459
Let's go.

51:29.252 --> 51:30.921
RESTRICTED AREA

51:31.004 --> 51:32.714
Excuse me.

51:32.798 --> 51:34.883
-Hello.
-Ma'am, could you lift your legs?

51:38.470 --> 51:42.682
Ma'am, I'm just going to check
to see if your water did break.

51:43.391 --> 51:45.268
It may feel slightly uncomfortable.

51:45.977 --> 51:47.145
It must have been a shock.

51:47.229 --> 51:49.439
Just leave it to us and relax.

51:49.523 --> 51:52.234
Both you and the baby will be fine.

51:53.944 --> 51:56.571
I put a line in,
and I requested a CBC and blood chemistry.

51:57.113 --> 51:59.407
And the patient
would like to go to her hospital--

51:59.491 --> 52:02.369
No, she can't go! She can't!

52:05.455 --> 52:07.082
The baby's umbilical cord is out!

52:07.165 --> 52:08.166
What?

52:08.250 --> 52:09.543
Call the professor! It's urgent!

52:11.253 --> 52:12.921
She needs to go to the OR now!

52:13.004 --> 52:15.048
-The transport driver.
-What?

52:15.131 --> 52:16.883
-Call them now! Hurry!
-Okay!

52:16.967 --> 52:19.094
Ma'am, the umbilical cord has fallen out,

52:19.177 --> 52:20.846
so we have to go into surgery now.

52:20.929 --> 52:22.514
Could you please come to the ER?

52:22.597 --> 52:24.808
Anesthesiology? We're bringing her up now.

52:24.891 --> 52:25.934
It's an emergency.

52:26.643 --> 52:28.520
We don't like it any more than you do!

52:28.603 --> 52:30.689
Pediatrics? We need to deliver a baby now.

52:31.523 --> 52:33.400
You can just come up right now yourself!

52:33.483 --> 52:34.568
Hurry!

52:35.360 --> 52:36.736
What are you doing? Quit staring!

52:36.820 --> 52:39.781
-Call the guardian and get consent now!
-Yes, ma'am!

52:39.865 --> 52:41.408
Are you okay, ma'am?

52:41.491 --> 52:43.034
Hang in there, ma'am.

52:43.118 --> 52:45.287
-We're going to move.
-I'll take a look. It's okay.

52:48.456 --> 52:51.042
Cervix is at 5.0.
There's been no change for two hours.

52:51.126 --> 52:52.669
Station's still at zero.

52:54.421 --> 52:57.132
As you prescribed,
starting oxytocin at 15.

52:59.134 --> 53:00.051
Are you okay?

53:00.927 --> 53:01.887
I'm fine.

53:03.513 --> 53:06.641
Dr. Oh, my request…

53:06.725 --> 53:07.934
What?

53:08.018 --> 53:09.686
Later, in the delivery room,

53:10.437 --> 53:11.980
have the interns observe.

53:12.063 --> 53:13.857
-I know. I won't forget.
-Especially…

53:15.734 --> 53:17.360
those who haven't seen a delivery yet.

53:17.444 --> 53:19.237
Yes, I'll take care of it.

53:19.946 --> 53:23.617
Wait! Make sure you set everything up,

53:23.700 --> 53:25.368
so they can see up close.

53:25.452 --> 53:27.078
That isn't what's important right now.

53:27.162 --> 53:28.371
Right from the incision,

53:28.455 --> 53:30.206
so they can properly see
from the beginning…

53:30.290 --> 53:31.124
Professor!

53:32.751 --> 53:34.794
I have a request too.

53:34.878 --> 53:35.712
Please…

53:36.963 --> 53:39.716
Please, can't you just focus
on the contractions?

53:40.592 --> 53:41.468
What?

53:42.928 --> 53:43.762
What did you say?

53:47.307 --> 53:48.516
I'll see you after I deliver.

53:53.146 --> 53:54.898
Son of a…

54:07.535 --> 54:08.370
Hello.

54:09.037 --> 54:10.872
We're going to administer the drug now.

54:11.456 --> 54:12.290
Now?

54:13.959 --> 54:15.377
She's asleep.

54:15.460 --> 54:17.545
I'll be back a bit later then.

54:18.171 --> 54:20.882
I'll return in about 30 minutes.

54:20.966 --> 54:21.841
That…

54:24.344 --> 54:25.971
What's wrong with that?

54:27.055 --> 54:28.139
Why is it red?

54:28.765 --> 54:29.933
Pardon?

54:31.977 --> 54:33.687
No, you can't!

54:35.647 --> 54:37.649
Don't give my sister that medicine!

54:38.274 --> 54:40.944
Give her a clear one instead.

54:41.027 --> 54:42.487
Like the one before.

54:42.570 --> 54:45.657
Not that one!

54:46.491 --> 54:48.994
But it's the drug
I explained to you last time.

54:49.077 --> 54:52.414
Mi-ja!

54:52.497 --> 54:55.792
Goodness, Mi-ja!

54:56.876 --> 54:59.004
You said you wouldn't die!

54:59.087 --> 55:01.339
You said you wanted to stay with me!

55:02.590 --> 55:05.468
Our parents are gone,
and I have no husband.

55:05.552 --> 55:07.595
If you leave me too,

55:08.638 --> 55:10.724
I really will be alone!

55:13.143 --> 55:16.312
Mi-ja! I'll be an orphan!

55:17.689 --> 55:20.442
Don't leave me, Mi-ja!

55:20.525 --> 55:23.903
Don't die, Mi-ja!

55:25.488 --> 55:27.907
Mi-ja!

55:29.117 --> 55:30.035
Mi-ja!

55:32.245 --> 55:35.415
Mi-ja!

55:36.875 --> 55:38.418
Mi-ja!

55:41.713 --> 55:42.797
Mi-ja.

55:43.840 --> 55:44.841
Here.

55:49.554 --> 55:51.473
Just be straight with me.

55:51.556 --> 55:52.724
I'm fine.

55:52.807 --> 55:55.977
Well, I'm not sure
what you want me to be straight about.

55:56.061 --> 55:57.812
I know everything.

55:58.396 --> 55:59.272
My sister…

56:01.441 --> 56:02.484
is dying.

56:03.193 --> 56:04.110
Sorry?

56:04.194 --> 56:06.946
That's why you put her near the door,

56:07.572 --> 56:09.908
so you can quickly check to see
if she's dead or not.

56:10.408 --> 56:11.576
That's why she moved.

56:11.659 --> 56:12.911
And did you see earlier?

56:13.912 --> 56:15.747
She's lucid and eating again.

56:16.831 --> 56:18.583
Before people die,

56:18.666 --> 56:21.586
they use up their last bit of strength.

56:22.545 --> 56:25.799
That's why they eat and walk like normal.

56:26.841 --> 56:28.343
It's not that though.

56:28.426 --> 56:29.928
Then what about that red drug?

56:30.011 --> 56:31.012
Red?

56:32.222 --> 56:33.306
The anti-cancer drug?

56:33.389 --> 56:35.809
That's what you give
when someone's about to die.

56:36.601 --> 56:38.561
You give it to a hopeless patient,

56:38.645 --> 56:41.189
so they can hold on for a few more days.

56:41.815 --> 56:43.650
You think I wouldn't know?

56:45.318 --> 56:47.320
They said that's how they all passed!

56:48.071 --> 56:49.489
At the bed by the door,

56:50.156 --> 56:52.909
they became fully lucid
and received that red drug.

56:54.619 --> 56:56.204
That's how they all died.

56:57.747 --> 56:58.915
That's not true.

56:59.707 --> 57:01.251
It really isn't.

57:02.710 --> 57:04.504
The bed really was broken.

57:04.587 --> 57:06.965
They're fixing it tonight, so you'll see.

57:08.424 --> 57:09.759
And she's eating well,

57:10.385 --> 57:12.178
because we drained the fluid
from her abdomen

57:12.262 --> 57:13.763
and adjusted her albumin.

57:13.847 --> 57:16.224
So her condition just improved greatly.

57:17.142 --> 57:18.393
And that red drug

57:18.476 --> 57:21.104
is used for recurrence,
so it's different from the other one.

57:21.187 --> 57:23.606
It's not for dying patients
or anything like that.

57:24.232 --> 57:25.108
Really?

57:26.025 --> 57:28.486
You're not just lying
in case I faint from shock?

57:28.570 --> 57:30.572
Why would I lie to you, ma'am?

57:32.490 --> 57:33.658
But

57:34.617 --> 57:36.995
where did you hear all that nonsense?

57:39.914 --> 57:41.583
That lady there.

57:43.084 --> 57:45.211
She said her friends all left like that.

57:46.838 --> 57:49.382
And she said my sister would die soon too.

57:55.388 --> 57:57.348
Oh, my God!

57:59.392 --> 58:00.768
What are you doing?

58:00.852 --> 58:03.021
-You can't just touch that!
-Yi-young!

58:03.605 --> 58:04.522
Don't turn it on.

58:04.606 --> 58:05.857
Turn the oxytocin off.

58:06.483 --> 58:07.567
Turn it off, damn it!

58:07.650 --> 58:10.153
What? You prescribed this yourself.

58:10.236 --> 58:11.154
I don't know.

58:12.530 --> 58:14.949
The epidural's not working
at all right now.

58:15.033 --> 58:16.159
Not at all.

58:18.203 --> 58:19.913
But these contractions need oxytocin.

58:19.996 --> 58:21.164
No!

58:22.290 --> 58:23.791
I'll be on call today.

58:23.875 --> 58:26.085
And then, I'll make the prescriptions.

58:26.169 --> 58:27.170
So turn the oxytocin off.

58:27.253 --> 58:28.838
Turn it off now!

58:29.506 --> 58:30.423
Okay, I will.

58:32.300 --> 58:33.301
Yi-young.

58:34.010 --> 58:36.346
Get me an OR.

58:36.429 --> 58:38.681
But, Professor,
I think you can wait a bit longer.

58:38.765 --> 58:40.934
No! I need surgery now!

58:41.976 --> 58:43.770
There's no change in the cervix at all.

58:44.771 --> 58:47.148
Let's just do the surgery, okay?

58:47.232 --> 58:48.566
Okay, Professor.

58:48.650 --> 58:49.984
I'll notify Professor Seo.

58:50.068 --> 58:52.320
No, I gave the order just now!

58:53.112 --> 58:54.572
Forget that and just get the OR.

58:55.949 --> 58:56.908
Anesthesiology!

58:57.534 --> 59:00.370
Are you in pain, ma'am?
Oh, dear, it must be awful.

59:01.079 --> 59:02.705
She's our professor…

59:02.789 --> 59:05.959
Ma'am, are you in a lot of pain?
You can't bear it?

59:06.042 --> 59:06.960
Who are you?

59:07.043 --> 59:09.045
I'm a new nurse here. It's okay, ma'am.

59:09.128 --> 59:10.380
Take a deep breath.

59:14.509 --> 59:16.344
You must have been in so much pain.

59:16.427 --> 59:18.513
The painkillers didn't work,
so it must really hurt.

59:19.138 --> 59:22.433
It's okay.
You're doing so well right now, Ms. Geum.

59:22.517 --> 59:24.519
The other mothers were crying and yelling,

59:24.602 --> 59:26.187
but you're doing so well.

59:26.271 --> 59:27.564
Doctor, an OR, please.

59:28.439 --> 59:30.024
Nurse, I don't think I can do it.

59:30.108 --> 59:31.734
-It hurts, doesn't it?
-It's so…

59:31.818 --> 59:34.028
It hurts so much. I had no idea it would!

59:35.113 --> 59:37.115
Anesthesiology? Is there a free OR?

59:40.118 --> 59:41.703
Make sure to check on the patient.

59:42.287 --> 59:43.121
Yes, ma'am.

59:44.330 --> 59:45.748
Still, it's a relief.

59:46.332 --> 59:48.126
The baby's saturation went up quick,

59:48.209 --> 59:49.794
and the mother didn't bleed much.

59:50.628 --> 59:51.671
Yeah, it was a relief.

59:54.924 --> 59:55.758
Tak Gi-on!

59:58.595 --> 59:59.637
He saw everything, right?

01:00:03.558 --> 01:00:05.768
I think we were screaming
like animals earlier.

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:06.686
Right?

01:00:07.478 --> 01:00:08.813
No wonder my throat's sore.

01:00:11.566 --> 01:00:14.235
Gosh, next year's going to be a tough one.

01:00:15.111 --> 01:00:18.239
I'll find out if there's another intern
we can persuade.

01:00:19.365 --> 01:00:20.617
Okay, let's find one.

01:00:22.619 --> 01:00:23.828
I'm sure we'll find one.

01:00:25.163 --> 01:00:26.080
Hey, Gi-on!

01:00:29.667 --> 01:00:31.628
Hey, what are you doing?
I've been calling you.

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:33.463
I'm looking something up.

01:00:33.546 --> 01:00:35.590
The patient
with the prolapsed cord earlier?

01:00:35.673 --> 01:00:36.507
Yeah.

01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:41.471
Holy cow.

01:00:42.472 --> 01:00:44.182
The baby and mother are fine.

01:00:44.265 --> 01:00:45.850
They must be in their room already.

01:00:48.436 --> 01:00:51.272
When I saw the OB doctors
screaming earlier,

01:00:51.356 --> 01:00:52.649
I thought the patient was dying.

01:00:53.900 --> 01:00:56.486
Man, OB is so scary.

01:00:58.237 --> 01:00:59.113
Really?

01:01:00.073 --> 01:01:01.449
I thought it was pretty awesome.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:07.997
-See you later.
-Bye.

01:01:10.583 --> 01:01:12.460
-Yi-young?
-Yes?

01:01:13.920 --> 01:01:16.381
When the uterine incision is made,

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:17.840
that's the most important part.

01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:22.428
She says to come closer to watch
without getting contaminated.

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:23.596
-Yes, Doctor.
-Yes, Doctor.

01:01:25.056 --> 01:01:27.433
Thanks, Dr. Oh.

01:01:27.517 --> 01:01:28.518
Ma'am.

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:31.229
Don't worry about anything else now,

01:01:31.312 --> 01:01:34.148
and just focus on the baby.
You're a mother now, not a professor.

01:01:34.232 --> 01:01:35.692
Yes, Professor.

01:01:36.818 --> 01:01:38.277
Let's get started.

01:01:38.361 --> 01:01:39.404
Excuse me, Professor?

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:42.156
Do you remember my request?

01:01:42.240 --> 01:01:43.908
You have to do it for me, okay?

01:01:43.991 --> 01:01:45.910
You really want to go through with it?

01:01:45.993 --> 01:01:46.953
Yes.

01:01:48.121 --> 01:01:50.039
Well, if that's what you want…

01:01:50.790 --> 01:01:51.999
Then that's what we'll do.

01:01:55.461 --> 01:01:56.838
Do you need something?

01:01:57.422 --> 01:01:58.256
No.

01:01:59.048 --> 01:02:02.176
We have a lot of eyes observing today.
I want you to stay focused.

01:02:02.927 --> 01:02:03.761
Yes, ma'am.

01:02:05.680 --> 01:02:06.514
Scalpel.

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:10.226
ANESTHESIA TIME, SURGERY TIME

01:02:10.309 --> 01:02:12.103
ANESTHESIA TIME, CURRENT TIME,
SURGERY TIME

01:02:12.186 --> 01:02:14.105
SURGERY TIME

01:02:14.188 --> 01:02:16.149
The baby's coming out.

01:02:23.322 --> 01:02:24.699
It's out!

01:02:24.782 --> 01:02:25.867
Hi!

01:02:25.950 --> 01:02:27.869
It's 4:15 p.m., and it's a baby girl.

01:02:31.456 --> 01:02:32.665
Ma'am,

01:02:32.749 --> 01:02:34.500
the baby's healthy.

01:02:35.293 --> 01:02:36.586
She's so beautiful.

01:02:37.170 --> 01:02:38.421
Thank you, Professor.

01:02:39.672 --> 01:02:43.176
Now, we'll deliver the placenta
and close up.

01:02:43.801 --> 01:02:45.052
You may feel some discomfort.

01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:48.681
Yi-young, I need you
to do something for me today.

01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:50.850
It was Professor Geum's wish

01:02:50.933 --> 01:02:53.811
for a first-year resident to close her up.

01:02:53.895 --> 01:02:54.896
What?

01:02:54.979 --> 01:02:55.980
Didn't you hear earlier?

01:02:56.063 --> 01:02:57.774
That was her last request.

01:02:59.776 --> 01:03:00.610
Oh, my God.

01:03:00.693 --> 01:03:03.946
There's no bleeding,
and the baby's healthy.

01:03:04.030 --> 01:03:06.282
We just need you to wrap things up now.

01:03:06.365 --> 01:03:08.159
I'm okay.

01:03:08.242 --> 01:03:10.870
I mean,
I think it'll be good if I don't do it.

01:03:10.953 --> 01:03:13.456
That's what I thought you'd say,
so I'm telling you now.

01:03:13.539 --> 01:03:14.540
We don't have time.

01:03:16.501 --> 01:03:19.253
Not everyone
gets a chance like this, Dr. Oh.

01:03:20.296 --> 01:03:21.798
I'm fine. Really.

01:03:22.840 --> 01:03:24.967
I'm scared. What if I mess up?

01:03:25.051 --> 01:03:27.512
Don't mess up then. We'll be watching.

01:03:28.095 --> 01:03:29.347
Just do as you've learned.

01:03:29.430 --> 01:03:30.723
Don't worry.

01:03:34.227 --> 01:03:36.187
Yi-young, take the lead.

01:03:55.706 --> 01:03:57.083
You'll have to do it someday.

01:03:57.166 --> 01:03:59.836
Aren't you here to be a doctor?
You can't be scared forever.

01:04:01.462 --> 01:04:02.755
Make a good edge,

01:04:02.839 --> 01:04:05.550
and you know you have to
avoid the endometrium to not damage it

01:04:05.633 --> 01:04:07.218
when you suture, right?

01:04:07.301 --> 01:04:09.053
I'll do my best to assist you.

01:04:10.137 --> 01:04:11.806
Don't worry and take the lead.

01:04:29.073 --> 01:04:30.074
Get started.

01:04:30.157 --> 01:04:32.994
Do-won, tie up where the incision starts.

01:04:33.077 --> 01:04:33.911
Yes, ma'am.

01:04:53.890 --> 01:04:55.766
Lift the thread up higher and pull.

01:04:56.601 --> 01:04:58.978
There you go. You're doing well.

01:05:07.570 --> 01:05:10.531
Dr. Oh, what should I do?

01:05:10.615 --> 01:05:12.241
Please pull a little harder.

01:05:15.036 --> 01:05:16.370
Yes, Doctor.

01:05:42.438 --> 01:05:43.981
Doctor.

01:05:45.024 --> 01:05:46.943
Yes? Are you all right?

01:05:47.526 --> 01:05:49.570
Did I do that again?

01:05:49.654 --> 01:05:52.198
Did I get confused and say nonsense?

01:05:53.616 --> 01:05:54.617
No, ma'am.

01:05:55.493 --> 01:05:56.661
You just

01:05:57.662 --> 01:06:00.873
briefly visited a few times
with some people you'd been missing.

01:06:02.500 --> 01:06:07.296
Then, right now,
I guess I wanted to see you.

01:06:09.840 --> 01:06:11.175
Doctor.

01:06:12.343 --> 01:06:15.304
While I'm still lucid,

01:06:16.222 --> 01:06:20.434
I'd like to ask you for just one favor.

01:06:21.227 --> 01:06:23.479
Would you be able to do that for me?

01:06:24.313 --> 01:06:25.147
What is it?

01:06:27.858 --> 01:06:31.028
No matter how much I say no,
you never listen, do you?

01:06:31.112 --> 01:06:33.614
Did you secretly find out
when you're going to die?

01:06:33.698 --> 01:06:37.284
You always ask to take a funeral photo.
What's so good about it?

01:06:37.368 --> 01:06:39.578
Gosh, you're so stubborn.

01:06:39.662 --> 01:06:42.915
It's my last goodbye to everyone.

01:06:43.666 --> 01:06:49.588
So it's better to take it while looking
as young and beautiful as possible.

01:06:49.672 --> 01:06:52.425
Beautiful? You're all old now.

01:06:57.221 --> 01:06:59.223
Since when did we become this old?

01:07:05.354 --> 01:07:07.898
You've become older than Mom, Mi-ja.

01:07:07.982 --> 01:07:13.029
That's because Mom passed when she was 50.

01:07:15.322 --> 01:07:16.449
But you're…

01:07:19.994 --> 01:07:23.289
My little sister is so beautiful.

01:07:23.873 --> 01:07:24.957
You are.

01:07:27.126 --> 01:07:28.377
I'm not!

01:07:29.879 --> 01:07:31.881
I'm 75 years old.

01:07:32.631 --> 01:07:37.928
Still, my little sister will forever
be beautiful in my eyes.

01:07:38.721 --> 01:07:39.555
You will.

01:07:41.015 --> 01:07:42.308
Let's hurry and take the photo!

01:07:42.892 --> 01:07:44.310
The doctor's busy too.

01:07:46.145 --> 01:07:46.979
Ma'am!

01:07:47.855 --> 01:07:50.566
You and the background.
Everything looks perfect.

01:07:54.320 --> 01:07:56.113
Where did you get a camera?

01:07:56.197 --> 01:07:58.407
From my bag. It has everything.

01:08:00.743 --> 01:08:02.536
Okay, here we go!

01:08:03.537 --> 01:08:04.455
Please look here.

01:08:05.581 --> 01:08:08.209
One, two, three!

01:08:08.793 --> 01:08:09.794
Wah-wah!

01:08:13.297 --> 01:08:14.340
It looks nice.

01:08:16.801 --> 01:08:20.179
I'll get this developed
and give it to you at the next treatment.

01:08:20.262 --> 01:08:22.098
Okay, thank you.

01:08:33.442 --> 01:08:34.610
Would you like one together?

01:08:35.402 --> 01:08:38.322
Forget it. We're too old for pictures.

01:08:39.281 --> 01:08:40.449
This is a good camera though.

01:08:41.492 --> 01:08:42.409
No, thanks.

01:08:42.493 --> 01:08:46.288
Come on, let's take a picture.
Just one. Please?

01:08:46.372 --> 01:08:48.207
I said it's okay.

01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:49.416
Come on, right now!

01:08:50.042 --> 01:08:51.710
I have a lot of work to get to.

01:08:51.794 --> 01:08:53.462
-I have to go soon. Hurry.
-Goodness…

01:08:58.259 --> 01:08:59.718
How lovely.

01:09:00.344 --> 01:09:01.804
You two look like young ladies.

01:09:04.181 --> 01:09:06.600
All right. Just relax and smile!

01:09:06.684 --> 01:09:07.643
Here I go!

01:09:15.401 --> 01:09:16.402
Let's take one more.

01:09:25.995 --> 01:09:26.954
Okay.

01:09:28.706 --> 01:09:31.167
One, two, three.

01:09:38.549 --> 01:09:40.843
She said she'd deliver her own baby.

01:09:41.886 --> 01:09:43.637
She underestimated the pain.

01:09:43.721 --> 01:09:45.347
Do you know how much it hurts?

01:09:45.973 --> 01:09:48.058
It's not like delivering a patient's baby.

01:09:49.643 --> 01:09:52.855
By the way,
do you think our age-old OB tradition

01:09:52.938 --> 01:09:54.231
will work on Yi-young too?

01:09:55.065 --> 01:09:57.484
"The OB professor's doctor
sticks with OB."

01:09:57.568 --> 01:09:58.944
You've never heard that before?

01:09:59.028 --> 01:09:59.945
I have.

01:10:00.029 --> 01:10:02.448
When my professor gave birth,
I was her doctor.

01:10:02.531 --> 01:10:04.867
Sae-byeok was my doctor
when I had Seok-hun.

01:10:04.950 --> 01:10:06.827
-When you had your second child?
-Yeah.

01:10:06.911 --> 01:10:09.371
We both considered joining GYN,

01:10:09.455 --> 01:10:10.873
but at our professors' deliveries,

01:10:10.956 --> 01:10:13.375
we sutured for the first time ever
and joined OB.

01:10:15.085 --> 01:10:17.171
I wonder if this tradition
will work again or not.

01:10:17.254 --> 01:10:18.839
Instead of tradition,

01:10:18.923 --> 01:10:20.758
I think food or sleep
would work on her more.

01:10:20.841 --> 01:10:21.675
Really?

01:10:22.468 --> 01:10:25.095
Then, to congratulate and persuade her,

01:10:25.679 --> 01:10:28.265
should we take her out
to eat something good?

01:10:28.849 --> 01:10:31.352
Do you think she'll be able to eat today?

01:10:33.854 --> 01:10:34.730
Right.

01:10:36.440 --> 01:10:38.359
She took the lead for the first time.

01:10:38.984 --> 01:10:41.987
She sutured the uterus
and closed up the patient on her own.

01:10:42.071 --> 01:10:44.823
Her heart's probably still pounding,

01:10:44.907 --> 01:10:46.408
so she can't even drink water.

01:10:46.492 --> 01:10:48.661
Right. Let's take her out next time.

01:10:49.954 --> 01:10:51.163
Gosh, Yi-young.

01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:55.209
Gosh, I bet she won't get
any sleep tonight.

01:11:05.970 --> 01:11:06.845
Yes?

01:11:09.139 --> 01:11:10.724
I was called, right? Right?

01:11:10.808 --> 01:11:11.642
What?

01:11:12.851 --> 01:11:14.520
I think Prof. Geum called me.

01:11:15.854 --> 01:11:17.481
Is she bleeding? Is she in pain?

01:11:18.148 --> 01:11:18.983
I didn't hear.

01:11:33.956 --> 01:11:35.165
Dr. Oh.

01:11:35.249 --> 01:11:37.835
How many times are you going to check?

01:11:38.794 --> 01:11:39.670
I'm just nervous.

01:11:40.546 --> 01:11:42.256
It was my first time suturing,

01:11:42.339 --> 01:11:44.925
and I think I pulled
too hard on the skin earlier.

01:11:46.969 --> 01:11:49.305
It's okay.
That's how you learn and get better.

01:11:53.559 --> 01:11:55.311
But did you pull really hard?

01:11:57.855 --> 01:11:59.481
Professor, I've never seen this before.

01:12:00.399 --> 01:12:02.985
I was in the OB ward for a year
at another hospital.

01:12:03.694 --> 01:12:06.030
But I've never seen
a dressing site this clean before.

01:12:07.656 --> 01:12:09.908
I'm the one who taught her
how to do stitches.

01:12:09.992 --> 01:12:11.410
I think you're okay.

01:12:16.832 --> 01:12:18.292
I'll be back in an hour

01:12:18.375 --> 01:12:20.002
to check for bleeding.

01:12:20.085 --> 01:12:22.546
You don't have to come back.
Let me sleep, please!

01:12:22.629 --> 01:12:23.756
I'll see you later!

01:12:23.839 --> 01:12:24.923
Goodness' sake.

01:12:29.720 --> 01:12:32.097
Were you unable to go home because of me?

01:12:32.890 --> 01:12:33.724
Yes.

01:12:35.059 --> 01:12:37.144
I'm sorry. You didn't have to stay.

01:12:39.146 --> 01:12:41.940
I could've gone home but didn't.

01:12:42.024 --> 01:12:43.400
I wanted to pay you back.

01:12:46.111 --> 01:12:48.697
Starting from today,
I wanted pay you back little by little.

01:12:49.615 --> 01:12:51.533
But I wasn't much help, right?

01:12:52.993 --> 01:12:54.370
It'll take ages to pay you back.

01:12:55.621 --> 01:12:57.414
No, you don't have to pay me back.

01:12:58.457 --> 01:12:59.708
There's no need for that.

01:13:17.142 --> 01:13:19.395
Okay, I'll take a look before we begin.

01:13:20.604 --> 01:13:23.107
Even with the numbing cream,
it might still sting.

01:13:23.190 --> 01:13:26.443
But please try not to move.

01:13:27.069 --> 01:13:28.779
If it hurts, raise your right hand.

01:13:29.696 --> 01:13:30.739
Okay?

01:13:36.954 --> 01:13:40.249
After that, I couldn't bring myself
to reach out to you.

01:13:41.667 --> 01:13:43.085
Because of me,

01:13:43.168 --> 01:13:45.629
rumors spread
that you punched a senior doctor.

01:13:47.089 --> 01:13:50.217
Baseless rumors usually spread fast.

01:13:50.300 --> 01:13:51.218
I know, right?

01:13:52.553 --> 01:13:55.139
You didn't punch him. You bit him.

01:14:00.978 --> 01:14:02.688
Hey, you crazy idiot!

01:14:02.771 --> 01:14:04.523
Ow! My hand!

01:14:05.149 --> 01:14:08.318
I need this hand for surgeries! Please!

01:14:08.402 --> 01:14:09.486
Okay!

01:14:11.905 --> 01:14:13.240
The skin clinic went under.

01:14:14.491 --> 01:14:16.660
It got bad reviews for poor quality.

01:14:20.539 --> 01:14:23.167
I think it started to get bad
after you bit his hand.

01:14:24.168 --> 01:14:25.252
That's why I bit him.

01:14:28.964 --> 01:14:31.216
After him, was there anyone else
who was like that?

01:14:32.259 --> 01:14:33.093
Of course not.

01:14:33.802 --> 01:14:35.846
These days, I do the touching.

01:14:37.347 --> 01:14:38.182
That's a relief.

01:14:44.563 --> 01:14:46.690
It's been an hour. I'll get going first.

01:14:47.316 --> 01:14:48.192
Where are you going?

01:14:48.275 --> 01:14:49.359
To see Prof. Geum.

01:14:50.152 --> 01:14:52.988
But she said not to.
She told you to go home now.

01:14:53.071 --> 01:14:54.281
I'm worried she might bleed.

01:14:54.364 --> 01:14:56.366
I'll just check one more time before I go.

01:14:59.953 --> 01:15:00.954
Wait for me, Doctor!

01:15:01.580 --> 01:15:02.789
You can go home!

01:15:02.873 --> 01:15:04.041
I'll come with you.

01:15:04.124 --> 01:15:05.250
Aren't you busy?

01:15:05.334 --> 01:15:06.585
I'm not.

01:15:15.594 --> 01:15:18.013
KU DO-WON
109/1404 DONGHAE APT, SINWOO-DONG, JUNG-GU

01:15:18.096 --> 01:15:19.973
Right, the address for the wedding gifts.

01:15:20.766 --> 01:15:24.019
OH YI-YOUNG
109/1404 DONGHAE APT, SINWOO-DONG, JUNG-GU

01:15:29.274 --> 01:15:31.527
PYO NAM-KYUNG

01:15:32.319 --> 01:15:33.153
Hey, Nam-kyung.

01:15:34.947 --> 01:15:36.740
A hot herbal tea for me.

01:15:36.823 --> 01:15:37.866
Hey, Yi-young and…

01:15:38.659 --> 01:15:40.661
Never mind. I'll tell you in the lounge.

01:15:41.495 --> 01:15:42.538
Okay, come quick.

01:15:48.001 --> 01:15:49.211
Dr. Ku?

01:15:49.753 --> 01:15:51.380
-Hi.
-It is you!

01:15:51.463 --> 01:15:53.173
I thought you were someone else.

01:15:53.757 --> 01:15:55.968
With that hat, you look like someone else.

01:15:56.051 --> 01:15:57.803
My hair was flattened by my surgical cap.

01:15:59.555 --> 01:16:00.389
Going somewhere?

01:16:00.973 --> 01:16:01.890
Out to eat.

01:16:01.974 --> 01:16:03.559
-Where?
-Near the hospital.

01:16:03.642 --> 01:16:04.935
With who?

01:16:05.018 --> 01:16:07.563
My sister-in-law. Why?
Want to know what we're eating too?

01:16:07.646 --> 01:16:08.814
No.

01:16:08.897 --> 01:16:11.066
I was wondering
if it was with your girlfriend.

01:16:12.985 --> 01:16:14.736
Instead of wondering
if I had a girlfriend,

01:16:14.820 --> 01:16:17.114
shouldn't you be more curious
about Seon Min-seon's BP?

01:16:17.781 --> 01:16:20.492
And without discharge notes,
we can't prescribe anything.

01:16:20.576 --> 01:16:21.451
So when will you…

01:16:22.202 --> 01:16:25.122
Oh, my. My coffee's getting cold.

01:16:25.205 --> 01:16:26.248
I'll get going.

01:16:28.625 --> 01:16:29.459
Hi!

01:16:31.837 --> 01:16:33.338
-Did you wait long?
-No.

01:16:33.422 --> 01:16:34.298
It's Joo-young.

01:16:34.381 --> 01:16:35.424
Are you okay to leave?

01:16:35.507 --> 01:16:36.925
Yeah. Aren't you cold?

01:16:37.009 --> 01:16:38.927
-They look too thin.
-No, I'm fine.

01:16:39.011 --> 01:16:42.222
That's Yi-young's sister.
Why did he say that's his sister-in-law?

01:16:51.398 --> 01:16:53.650
Dr. Cha thinks this is Dr. Ku.

01:16:53.734 --> 01:16:56.612
It could be him. Or not.

01:16:57.571 --> 01:17:01.033
Hey, think of him as Dr. Ku and look.

01:17:02.284 --> 01:17:03.827
HELP US FIND THIS MAN WHO SAVED A LIFE

01:17:04.620 --> 01:17:06.538
It is. I think it's him!

01:17:08.498 --> 01:17:09.666
Or maybe not.

01:17:09.750 --> 01:17:11.752
Hey! I have something big to tell you!

01:17:11.835 --> 01:17:13.920
-This is huge!
-Hey, this is bigger. Look.

01:17:14.004 --> 01:17:15.047
No, this isn't important.

01:17:15.130 --> 01:17:16.965
No, this is more important. Look at this.

01:17:17.049 --> 01:17:18.258
Doesn't he look like Dr. Ku?

01:17:18.342 --> 01:17:20.135
-Hey, that's…
-What?

01:17:20.802 --> 01:17:21.678
That is Dr. Ku.

01:17:21.762 --> 01:17:23.388
Really? How could you tell right away?

01:17:23.972 --> 01:17:26.141
The hat. That's Dr. Ku.

01:17:28.477 --> 01:17:29.770
It really must be him.

01:17:31.730 --> 01:17:32.856
Who's the woman with him?

01:17:33.482 --> 01:17:35.150
She aided like a professional.

01:17:35.692 --> 01:17:36.943
Is she from our hospital?

01:17:38.487 --> 01:17:40.072
I've seen those clothes before.

01:17:47.871 --> 01:17:49.581
You're right! It's Yi-young!

01:17:49.665 --> 01:17:51.166
It is her!

01:17:51.249 --> 01:17:52.959
It is them! The two of them!

01:17:53.043 --> 01:17:54.503
What? Hey!

01:17:55.587 --> 01:17:56.505
How did you know?

01:17:56.588 --> 01:17:57.714
You knew too?

01:17:57.798 --> 01:18:00.258
Yeah, I found out by coincidence.

01:18:00.342 --> 01:18:02.511
But I thought I should wait
until they told us.

01:18:02.594 --> 01:18:03.804
Hey, you traitors.

01:18:03.887 --> 01:18:05.764
You knew, but why didn't you tell me?

01:18:05.847 --> 01:18:07.641
Hey, how did you know?

01:18:07.724 --> 01:18:08.600
Did you see too?

01:18:09.351 --> 01:18:10.435
Yeah, I did. They're…

01:18:11.853 --> 01:18:12.854
-Living together.
-Dating?

01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:14.314
In-laws?

01:18:15.899 --> 01:18:18.151
Wait, hold on…

01:18:18.235 --> 01:18:19.152
What did you just say?

01:18:19.236 --> 01:18:20.278
You said they're what?

01:18:20.362 --> 01:18:21.488
I don't know.

01:18:21.571 --> 01:18:23.323
Wait, hold on. So…

01:18:23.407 --> 01:18:24.282
They're in-laws, but…

01:18:24.366 --> 01:18:25.242
They live together.

01:18:26.076 --> 01:18:27.202
And they're dating?

01:18:27.285 --> 01:18:28.245
-What?
-What?

01:18:28.745 --> 01:18:29.871
What?

01:18:30.539 --> 01:18:31.748
What are you talking about?

01:18:31.832 --> 01:18:32.874
That doesn't make sense.

01:18:32.958 --> 01:18:35.836
They're in-laws, so they could
live together for various reasons.

01:18:35.919 --> 01:18:38.046
But they wouldn't date.

01:18:39.756 --> 01:18:40.590
What?

01:18:43.927 --> 01:18:46.847
But why are they wearing the same shoes?

01:18:47.681 --> 01:18:50.517
Was it a group purchase
because they live together?

01:19:17.836 --> 01:19:19.504
I'm off to have lunch with my sister.

01:19:20.672 --> 01:19:21.506
Hey, Yi-young!

01:19:22.215 --> 01:19:23.049
What?

01:19:23.133 --> 01:19:25.260
-It's true!
-Oh, my God, Yi-young!

01:19:25.343 --> 01:19:26.261
Hey!

01:19:26.344 --> 01:19:27.512
You…

01:19:31.099 --> 01:19:32.017
What is it?

01:19:34.060 --> 01:19:35.145
What?

01:20:20.941 --> 01:20:24.945
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST,
JUNG MOON-SUNG, OUR ETERNAL DO JAE-HAK

01:20:25.529 --> 01:20:28.782
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:20:29.616 --> 01:20:32.369
I'll give birth
on January 1st at midnight.

01:20:32.452 --> 01:20:34.663
I said not yet!

01:20:34.746 --> 01:20:37.415
-Ma'am.
-Can we wait a bit?

01:20:37.499 --> 01:20:39.543
The baby's the one
who chooses when to come out.

01:20:40.502 --> 01:20:41.419
Doctor.

01:20:41.503 --> 01:20:42.420
What is it?

01:20:43.505 --> 01:20:46.091
Have you decided
on who the new OR professor will be?

01:20:46.174 --> 01:20:48.051
Our new OB professor will be…

01:20:48.134 --> 01:20:49.135
Yes, Professor.

01:20:49.636 --> 01:20:51.137
-So?
-For real?

01:20:51.221 --> 01:20:52.514
You two are…

01:20:52.597 --> 01:20:53.849
We're dating. Happy now?

01:20:53.932 --> 01:20:55.100
You'll be double in-laws?

01:20:55.684 --> 01:20:56.935
There's another couple?

01:20:57.018 --> 01:20:59.145
It's such a shame. If I had a daughter…

01:20:59.229 --> 01:21:00.772
Even if you did, it wouldn't matter.

01:21:00.856 --> 01:21:02.107
A secret relationship, my foot.

01:21:04.317 --> 01:21:06.152
When did I buy this?

01:21:07.279 --> 01:21:08.780
I'm not doing my second year.

01:21:08.864 --> 01:21:10.365
People like her stay the longest.

01:21:10.448 --> 01:21:11.700
It's her habit of speaking now.

01:21:11.783 --> 01:21:13.994
I wasn't going to tell you this, but…

01:21:14.077 --> 01:21:15.328
Ta-da!

01:21:23.336 --> 01:21:25.338
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
